{"surah": 37, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "وَٱلصَّٰٓفَّٰتِ صَفًّا ", "translation": "By those [angels] lined up in rows", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلصَّٰٓفَّٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَّٰfَّٰٓṣlٱَw", "root": "صفف"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "صَفًّا", "translit": "āًّfَṣ", "root": "صفف"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "فَٱلزَّٰجِرَٰتِ زَجْرًا ", "translation": "And those who drive [the clouds]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱلزَّٰجِرَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰrِjgَّٰzlٱَf", "root": "زجر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "زَجْرًا", "translit": "āًrْjgَz", "root": "زجر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "فَٱلتَّٰلِيَٰتِ ذِكْرًا ", "translation": "And those who recite the message,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱلتَّٰلِيَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰyِlَّٰtlٱَf", "root": "تلو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ذِكْرًا", "translit": "āًrْkِhd", "root": "ذكر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "إِنَّ إِلَٰهَكُمْ لَوَٰحِدٌ ", "translation": "Indeed, your God is One,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِلَٰهَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَhَٰlِiʾ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَوَٰحِدٌ", "translit": "ٌdِḥَٰwَl", "root": "وحد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "رَّبُّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا وَرَبُّ ٱلْمَشَٰرِقِ ", "translation": "Lord of the heavens and the earth and that between them and Lord of the sunrises.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "رَّبُّ", "translit": "ُّbَّr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰwَٰmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱَw", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بَيْنَهُمَا", "translit": "āَmُhَnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَرَبُّ", "translit": "ُّbَrَw", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْمَشَٰرِقِ", "translit": "ِqِrَٰhsَmْlٱ", "root": "شرق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "إِنَّا زَيَّنَّا ٱلسَّمَآءَ ٱلدُّنْيَا بِزِينَةٍ ٱلْكَوَاكِبِ ", "translation": "Indeed, We have adorned the nearest heaven with an adornment of stars", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "زَيَّنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَّyَz", "root": "زين"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلدُّنْيَا", "translit": "āَyْnُّdlٱ", "root": "دنو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِزِينَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَnyِzِb", "root": "زين"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْكَوَاكِبِ", "translit": "ِbِkāَwَkْlٱ", "root": "كوكب"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "وَحِفْظًا مِّن كُلِّ شَيْطَٰنٍ مَّارِدٍ ", "translation": "And as protection against every rebellious devil", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَحِفْظًا", "translit": "āًẓْfِḥَw", "root": "حفظ"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "شَيْطَٰنٍ", "translit": "ٍnَٰṭْyَhs", "root": "شطن"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَّارِدٍ", "translit": "ٍdِrāَّm", "root": "مرد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "لَّا يَسَّمَّعُونَ إِلَى ٱلْمَلَإِ ٱلْأَعْلَىٰ وَيُقْذَفُونَ مِن كُلِّ جَانِبٍ ", "translation": "[So] they may not listen to the exalted assembly [of angels] and are pelted from every side,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَّا", "translit": "āَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَسَّمَّعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعَّmَّsَy", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمَلَإِ", "translit": "ِiʾَlَmْlٱ", "root": "ملا"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْأَعْلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlْʿعَaʾْlٱ", "root": "علو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَيُقْذَفُونَ", "translit": "َnwُfَhdْqُyَw", "root": "قذف"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "جَانِبٍ", "translit": "ٍbِnāَjg", "root": "جنب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "دُحُورًاۖ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ وَاصِبٌ ", "translation": "Repelled; and for them is a constant punishment,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "دُحُورًا", "translit": "āًrwُḥُd", "root": "دحر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَلَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَذَابٌ", "translit": "ٌbāَhdَʿع", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَاصِبٌ", "translit": "ٌbِṣāَw", "root": "وصب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "إِلَّا مَنْ خَطِفَ ٱلْخَطْفَةَ فَأَتْبَعَهُۥ شِهَابٌ ثَاقِبٌ ", "translation": "Except one who snatches [some words] by theft, but they are pursued by a burning flame, piercing [in brightness].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَنْ", "translit": "ْnَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "خَطِفَ", "translit": "َfِṭَhk", "root": "خطف"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْخَطْفَةَ", "translit": "َẗَfْṭَhkْlٱ", "root": "خطف"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَأَتْبَعَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَʿعَbْtَaʾَf", "root": "تبع"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "شِهَابٌ", "translit": "ٌbāَhِhs", "root": "شهب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ثَاقِبٌ", "translit": "ٌbِqāَht", "root": "ثقب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "فَٱسْتَفْتِهِمْ أَهُمْ أَشَدُّ خَلْقًا أَم مَّنْ خَلَقْنَآۚ إِنَّا خَلَقْنَٰهُم مِّن طِينٍ لَّازِبٍۭ ", "translation": "Then inquire of them, [O Muḥammad], \"Are they a stronger [or more difficult] creation or those [others] We have created?\" Indeed, We created them [i.e., men] from sticky clay.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱسْتَفْتِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِtْfَtْsٱَf", "root": "فتي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَشَدُّ", "translit": "ُّdَhsَaʾ", "root": "شدد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "خَلْقًا", "translit": "āًqْlَhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَم", "translit": "mَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مَّنْ", "translit": "ْnَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "خَلَقْنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnْqَlَhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "خَلَقْنَٰهُم", "translit": "mُhَٰnْqَlَhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "طِينٍ", "translit": "ٍnyِṭ", "root": "طين"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لَّازِبٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭbِzāَّl", "root": "لزب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 12, "text": "بَلْ عَجِبْتَ وَيَسْخَرُونَ ", "translation": "But you wonder, while they mock,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "بَلْ", "translit": "ْlَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَجِبْتَ", "translit": "َtْbِjgَʿع", "root": "عجب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَيَسْخَرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrَhkْsَyَw", "root": "سخر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 13, "text": "وَإِذَا ذُكِّرُوا۟ لَا يَذْكُرُونَ ", "translation": "And when they are reminded, they remember not.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ذُكِّرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrِّkُhd", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَذْكُرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrُkْhdَy", "root": "ذكر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 14, "text": "وَإِذَا رَأَوْا۟ ءَايَةً يَسْتَسْخِرُونَ ", "translation": "And when they see a sign, they ridicule.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَأَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَaʾَr", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَايَةً", "translit": "ًẗَyāَء", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَسْتَسْخِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِhkْsَtْsَy", "root": "سخر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 15, "text": "وَقَالُوٓا۟ إِنْ هَٰذَآ إِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّبِينٌ ", "translation": "And say, \"This is not but obvious magic.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "هَٰذَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "سِحْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْḥِs", "root": "سحر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مُّبِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِbُّm", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 16, "text": "أَءِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَعِظَٰمًا أَءِنَّا لَمَبْعُوثُونَ ", "translation": "When we have died and become dust and bones, are we indeed to be resurrected?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَءِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِءَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِتْنَا", "translit": "āَnْtِm", "root": "موت"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَكُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُkَw", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تُرَابًا", "translit": "āًbāَrُt", "root": "ترب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَعِظَٰمًا", "translit": "āًmَٰẓِʿعَw", "root": "عظم"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَءِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِءَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَمَبْعُوثُونَ", "translit": "َnwُhtwُʿعْbَmَl", "root": "بعث"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 17, "text": "أَوَءَابَآؤُنَا ٱلْأَوَّلُونَ ", "translation": "And our forefathers [as well]?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَوَءَابَآؤُنَا", "translit": "āَnُwʾٓāَbāَءَwَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْأَوَّلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَّwَaʾْlٱ", "root": "اول"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 18, "text": "قُلْ نَعَمْ وَأَنتُمْ دَٰخِرُونَ ", "translation": "Say, \"Yes, and you will be [rendered] contemptible.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَعَمْ", "translit": "ْmَʿعَn", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَأَنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "دَٰخِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِhkَٰd", "root": "دخر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 19, "text": "فَإِنَّمَا هِىَ زَجْرَةٌ وَٰحِدَةٌ فَإِذَا هُمْ يَنظُرُونَ ", "translation": "It will be only one shout, and at once they will be observing.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَإِنَّمَا", "translit": "āَmَّnِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هِىَ", "translit": "َàِh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "زَجْرَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَrْjgَz", "root": "زجر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَٰحِدَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَdِḥَٰw", "root": "وحد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "هُمْ", "translit": "ْmُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَنظُرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrُẓnَy", "root": "نظر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 20, "text": "وَقَالُوا۟ يَٰوَيْلَنَا هَٰذَا يَوْمُ ٱلدِّينِ ", "translation": "They will say, \"O woe to us! This is the Day of Recompense.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَٰوَيْلَنَا", "translit": "āَnَlْyَwَٰy", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "هَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَوْمُ", "translit": "ُmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلدِّينِ", "translit": "ِnyِّdlٱ", "root": "دين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 21, "text": "هَٰذَا يَوْمُ ٱلْفَصْلِ ٱلَّذِى كُنتُم بِهِۦ تُكَذِّبُونَ ", "translation": "[They will be told], \"This is the Day of Judgement which you used to deny.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "هَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَوْمُ", "translit": "ُmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْفَصْلِ", "translit": "ِlْṣَfْlٱ", "root": "فصل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كُنتُم", "translit": "mُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "تُكَذِّبُونَ", "translit": "َnwُbِّhdَkُt", "root": "كذب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 22, "text": "ٱحْشُرُوا۟ ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا۟ وَأَزْوَٰجَهُمْ وَمَا كَانُوا۟ يَعْبُدُونَ ", "translation": "[The angels will be ordered], \"Gather those who committed wrong, their kinds,[1] and what they used to worship", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱحْشُرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrُhsْḥٱ", "root": "حشر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ظَلَمُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُmَlَẓ", "root": "ظلم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَأَزْوَٰجَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَjgَٰwْzَaʾَw", "root": "زوج"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَعْبُدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdُbْʿعَy", "root": "عبد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 23, "text": "مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ فَٱهْدُوهُمْ إِلَىٰ صِرَٰطِ ٱلْجَحِيمِ ", "translation": "Other than Allāh, and guide them to the path of Hellfire", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "دُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُd", "root": "دون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَٱهْدُوهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhwُdْhٱَf", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "صِرَٰطِ", "translit": "ِṭَٰrِṣ", "root": "صرط"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْجَحِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِḥَjgْlٱ", "root": "جحم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 24, "text": "وَقِفُوهُمْۖ إِنَّهُم مَّسْـُٔولُونَ ", "translation": "And stop them; indeed, they are to be questioned.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقِفُوهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhwُfِqَw", "root": "وقف"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّهُم", "translit": "mُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَّسْـُٔولُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlwُٔـْsَّm", "root": "سال"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 25, "text": "مَا لَكُمْ لَا تَنَاصَرُونَ ", "translation": "[They will be asked], \"What is [wrong] with you? Why do you not help each other?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَنَاصَرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrَṣāَnَt", "root": "نصر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 26, "text": "بَلْ هُمُ ٱلْيَوْمَ مُسْتَسْلِمُونَ ", "translation": "But they, that Day, are in surrender.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "بَلْ", "translit": "ْlَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هُمُ", "translit": "ُmُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْيَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَyْlٱ", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مُسْتَسْلِمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmِlْsَtْsُm", "root": "سلم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 27, "text": "وَأَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ يَتَسَآءَلُونَ ", "translation": "And they will approach one another asking [i.e., blaming] each other.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَقْبَلَ", "translit": "َlَbْqَaʾَw", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَعْضُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُḍْʿعَb", "root": "بعض"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بَعْضٍ", "translit": "ٍḍْʿعَb", "root": "بعض"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَتَسَآءَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَءٓāَsَtَy", "root": "سال"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 28, "text": "قَالُوٓا۟ إِنَّكُمْ كُنتُمْ تَأْتُونَنَا عَنِ ٱلْيَمِينِ ", "translation": "They will say, \"Indeed, you used to come at us from the right.\"[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كُنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَأْتُونَنَا", "translit": "āَnَnwُtْaʾَt", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَنِ", "translit": "ِnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْيَمِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِmَyْlٱ", "root": "يمن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 29, "text": "قَالُوا۟ بَل لَّمْ تَكُونُوا۟ مُؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "They [i.e., the oppressors] will say, \"Rather, you [yourselves] were not believers,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَل", "translit": "lَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَّمْ", "translit": "ْmَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَكُونُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnwُkَt", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مُؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُm", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 30, "text": "وَمَا كَانَ لَنَا عَلَيْكُم مِّن سُلْطَٰنٍۭۖ بَلْ كُنتُمْ قَوْمًا طَٰغِينَ ", "translation": "And we had over you no authority, but you were a transgressing people.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَنَا", "translit": "āَnَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَلَيْكُم", "translit": "mُkْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "سُلْطَٰنٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭnَٰṭْlُs", "root": "سلط"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بَلْ", "translit": "ْlَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كُنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "قَوْمًا", "translit": "āًmْwَq", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "طَٰغِينَ", "translit": "َnyِغَٰṭ", "root": "طغي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 31, "text": "فَحَقَّ عَلَيْنَا قَوْلُ رَبِّنَآۖ إِنَّا لَذَآئِقُونَ ", "translation": "So the word [i.e., decree] of our Lord has come into effect upon us; indeed, we will taste [punishment].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَحَقَّ", "translit": "َّqَḥَf", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْنَا", "translit": "āَnْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قَوْلُ", "translit": "ُlْwَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "رَبِّنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَذَآئِقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqِyʾٓāَhdَl", "root": "ذوق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 32, "text": "فَأَغْوَيْنَٰكُمْ إِنَّا كُنَّا غَٰوِينَ ", "translation": "And we led you to deviation; indeed, we were deviators.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَغْوَيْنَٰكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَٰnْyَwْغَaʾَf", "root": "غوي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "غَٰوِينَ", "translit": "َnyِwَٰغ", "root": "غوي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 33, "text": "فَإِنَّهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ فِى ٱلْعَذَابِ مُشْتَرِكُونَ ", "translation": "So indeed they, that Day, will be sharing in the punishment.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَإِنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَوْمَئِذٍ", "translit": "ٍhdِyʾَmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَذَابِ", "translit": "ِbāَhdَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مُشْتَرِكُونَ", "translit": "َnwُkِrَtْhsُm", "root": "شرك"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 34, "text": "إِنَّا كَذَٰلِكَ نَفْعَلُ بِٱلْمُجْرِمِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed, that is how We deal with the criminals.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَفْعَلُ", "translit": "ُlَʿعْfَn", "root": "فعل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِٱلْمُجْرِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِrْjgُmْlٱِb", "root": "جرم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 35, "text": "إِنَّهُمْ كَانُوٓا۟ إِذَا قِيلَ لَهُمْ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا ٱللَّهُ يَسْتَكْبِرُونَ ", "translation": "Indeed they, when it was said to them, \"There is no deity but Allāh,\" were arrogant", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَانُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قِيلَ", "translit": "َlyِq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَآ", "translit": "ٓāَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِلَٰهَ", "translit": "َhَٰlِiʾ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "يَسْتَكْبِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِbْkَtْsَy", "root": "كبر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 36, "text": "وَيَقُولُونَ أَئِنَّا لَتَارِكُوٓا۟ ءَالِهَتِنَا لِشَاعِرٍ مَّجْنُونٍۭ ", "translation": "And were saying, \"Are we to leave our gods for a mad poet?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيَقُولُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlwُqَyَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَئِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِyʾَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَتَارِكُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُkِrāَtَl", "root": "ترك"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ءَالِهَتِنَا", "translit": "āَnِtَhِlāَء", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لِشَاعِرٍ", "translit": "ٍrِʿعāَhsِl", "root": "شعر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مَّجْنُونٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭnwُnْjgَّm", "root": "جنن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 37, "text": "بَلْ جَآءَ بِٱلْحَقِّ وَصَدَّقَ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ ", "translation": "Rather, he [i.e., the Prophet (ﷺ)] has come with the truth and confirmed the [previous] messengers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "بَلْ", "translit": "ْlَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِٱلْحَقِّ", "translit": "ِّqَḥْlٱِb", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَصَدَّقَ", "translit": "َqَّdَṣَw", "root": "صدق"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَsْrُmْlٱ", "root": "رسل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 38, "text": "إِنَّكُمْ لَذَآئِقُوا۟ ٱلْعَذَابِ ٱلْأَلِيمِ ", "translation": "Indeed, you [disbelievers] will be tasters of the painful punishment,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَذَآئِقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqِyʾٓāَhdَl", "root": "ذوق"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْعَذَابِ", "translit": "ِbāَhdَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْأَلِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِlَaʾْlٱ", "root": "الم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 39, "text": "وَمَا تُجْزَوْنَ إِلَّا مَا كُنتُمْ تَعْمَلُونَ ", "translation": "And you will not be recompensed except for what you used to do -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تُجْزَوْنَ", "translit": "َnْwَzْjgُt", "root": "جزي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كُنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تَعْمَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَmْʿعَt", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 40, "text": "إِلَّا عِبَادَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلْمُخْلَصِينَ ", "translation": "But not the chosen servants of Allāh.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عِبَادَ", "translit": "َdāَbِʿع", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُخْلَصِينَ", "translit": "َnyِṣَlْhkُmْlٱ", "root": "خلص"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 41, "text": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ رِزْقٌ مَّعْلُومٌ ", "translation": "Those will have a provision determined -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رِزْقٌ", "translit": "ٌqْzِr", "root": "رزق"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَّعْلُومٌ", "translit": "ٌmwُlْʿعَّm", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 42, "text": "فَوَٰكِهُۖ وَهُم مُّكْرَمُونَ ", "translation": "Fruits;[1] and they will be honored", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَوَٰكِهُ", "translit": "ُhِkَٰwَf", "root": "فكه"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَهُم", "translit": "mُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مُّكْرَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَrْkُّm", "root": "كرم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 43, "text": "فِى جَنَّٰتِ ٱلنَّعِيمِ ", "translation": "In gardens of pleasure", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جَنَّٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَّٰnَjg", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلنَّعِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِʿعَّnlٱ", "root": "نعم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 44, "text": "عَلَىٰ سُرُرٍ مُّتَقَٰبِلِينَ ", "translation": "On thrones facing one another.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "سُرُرٍ", "translit": "ٍrُrُs", "root": "سرر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مُّتَقَٰبِلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlِbَٰqَtُّm", "root": "قبل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 45, "text": "يُطَافُ عَلَيْهِم بِكَأْسٍ مِّن مَّعِينٍۭ ", "translation": "There will be circulated among them a cup [of wine] from a flowing spring,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يُطَافُ", "translit": "ُfāَṭُy", "root": "طوف"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِم", "translit": "mِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِكَأْسٍ", "translit": "ٍsْaʾَkِb", "root": "كاس"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَّعِينٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭnyِʿعَّm", "root": "عين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 46, "text": "بَيْضَآءَ لَذَّةٍ لِّلشَّٰرِبِينَ ", "translation": "White and delicious to the drinkers;", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "بَيْضَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَḍْyَb", "root": "بيض"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَذَّةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَّhdَl", "root": "لذذ"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِّلشَّٰرِبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbِrَّٰhslِّl", "root": "شرب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 47, "text": "لَا فِيهَا غَوْلٌ وَلَا هُمْ عَنْهَا يُنزَفُونَ ", "translation": "No bad effect is there in it, nor from it will they be intoxicated.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "غَوْلٌ", "translit": "ٌlْwَغ", "root": "غول"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "هُمْ", "translit": "ْmُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَنْهَا", "translit": "āَhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يُنزَفُونَ", "translit": "َnwُfَznُy", "root": "نزف"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 48, "text": "وَعِندَهُمْ قَٰصِرَٰتُ ٱلطَّرْفِ عِينٌ ", "translation": "And with them will be women limiting [their] glances,[1] with large, [beautiful] eyes,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَعِندَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَdnِʿعَw", "root": "عند"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَٰصِرَٰتُ", "translit": "ُtَٰrِṣَٰq", "root": "قصر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلطَّرْفِ", "translit": "ِfْrَّṭlٱ", "root": "طرف"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِʿع", "root": "عين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 49, "text": "كَأَنَّهُنَّ بَيْضٌ مَّكْنُونٌ ", "translation": "As if they were [delicate] eggs, well-protected.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "كَأَنَّهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhَّnَaʾَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَيْضٌ", "translit": "ٌḍْyَb", "root": "بيض"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَّكْنُونٌ", "translit": "ٌnwُnْkَّm", "root": "كنن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 50, "text": "فَأَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ يَتَسَآءَلُونَ ", "translation": "And they will approach one another, inquiring of each other.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَقْبَلَ", "translit": "َlَbْqَaʾَf", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَعْضُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُḍْʿعَb", "root": "بعض"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بَعْضٍ", "translit": "ٍḍْʿعَb", "root": "بعض"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَتَسَآءَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَءٓāَsَtَy", "root": "سال"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 51, "text": "قَالَ قَآئِلٌ مِّنْهُمْ إِنِّى كَانَ لِى قَرِينٌ ", "translation": "A speaker among them will say, \"Indeed, I had a companion [on earth].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَآئِلٌ", "translit": "ٌlِyʾٓāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِّنْهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لِى", "translit": "àِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "قَرِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِrَq", "root": "قرن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 52, "text": "يَقُولُ أَءِنَّكَ لَمِنَ ٱلْمُصَدِّقِينَ ", "translation": "Who would say, 'Are you indeed of those who believe", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَقُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُqَy", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَءِنَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّnِءَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَمِنَ", "translit": "َnِmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُصَدِّقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِّdَṣُmْlٱ", "root": "صدق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 53, "text": "أَءِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَعِظَٰمًا أَءِنَّا لَمَدِينُونَ ", "translation": "That when we have died and become dust and bones, we will indeed be recompensed?'\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَءِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِءَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِتْنَا", "translit": "āَnْtِm", "root": "موت"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَكُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُkَw", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تُرَابًا", "translit": "āًbāَrُt", "root": "ترب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَعِظَٰمًا", "translit": "āًmَٰẓِʿعَw", "root": "عظم"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَءِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِءَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَمَدِينُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnyِdَmَl", "root": "دين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 54, "text": "قَالَ هَلْ أَنتُم مُّطَّلِعُونَ ", "translation": "He will say,[1] \"Would you [care to] look?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هَلْ", "translit": "ْlَh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَنتُم", "translit": "mُtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مُّطَّلِعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعِlَّṭُّm", "root": "طلع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 55, "text": "فَٱطَّلَعَ فَرَءَاهُ فِى سَوَآءِ ٱلْجَحِيمِ ", "translation": "And he will look and see him[1] in the midst of the Hellfire.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱطَّلَعَ", "translit": "َʿعَlَّṭٱَf", "root": "طلع"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَرَءَاهُ", "translit": "ُhāَءَrَf", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "سَوَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَwَs", "root": "سوي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْجَحِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِḥَjgْlٱ", "root": "جحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 56, "text": "قَالَ تَٱللَّهِ إِن كِدتَّ لَتُرْدِينِ ", "translation": "He will say, \"By Allāh, you almost ruined me.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱَt", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كِدتَّ", "translit": "َّtdِk", "root": "كود"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَتُرْدِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِdْrُtَl", "root": "ردي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 57, "text": "وَلَوْلَا نِعْمَةُ رَبِّى لَكُنتُ مِنَ ٱلْمُحْضَرِينَ ", "translation": "If not for the favor of my Lord, I would have been of those brought in [to Hell].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَوْلَا", "translit": "āَlْwَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نِعْمَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَmْʿعِn", "root": "نعم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبِّى", "translit": "àِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَكُنتُ", "translit": "ُtnُkَl", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْمُحْضَرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrَḍْḥُmْlٱ", "root": "حضر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 58, "text": "أَفَمَا نَحْنُ بِمَيِّتِينَ ", "translation": "Then, are we not to die", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَفَمَا", "translit": "āَmَfَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَحْنُ", "translit": "ُnْḥَn", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِمَيِّتِينَ", "translit": "َnyِtِّyَmِb", "root": "موت"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 59, "text": "إِلَّا مَوْتَتَنَا ٱلْأُولَىٰ وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمُعَذَّبِينَ ", "translation": "Except for our first death, and we will not be punished?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَوْتَتَنَا", "translit": "āَnَtَtْwَm", "root": "موت"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْأُولَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlwُaʾْlٱ", "root": "اول"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "نَحْنُ", "translit": "ُnْḥَn", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِمُعَذَّبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbَّhdَʿعُmِb", "root": "عذب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 60, "text": "إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَهُوَ ٱلْفَوْزُ ٱلْعَظِيمُ ", "translation": "Indeed, this is the great attainment.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْفَوْزُ", "translit": "ُzْwَfْlٱ", "root": "فوز"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْعَظِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِẓَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عظم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 61, "text": "لِمِثْلِ هَٰذَا فَلْيَعْمَلِ ٱلْعَٰمِلُونَ ", "translation": "For the like of this let the workers [on earth] work.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لِمِثْلِ", "translit": "ِlْhtِmِl", "root": "مثل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَلْيَعْمَلِ", "translit": "ِlَmْʿعَyْlَf", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَٰمِلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlِmَٰʿعْlٱ", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 62, "text": "أَذَٰلِكَ خَيْرٌ نُّزُلًا أَمْ شَجَرَةُ ٱلزَّقُّومِ ", "translation": "Is that [i.e., Paradise] a better accommodation or the tree of zaqqūm?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "خَيْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْyَhk", "root": "خير"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نُّزُلًا", "translit": "āًlُzُّn", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "شَجَرَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَrَjgَhs", "root": "شجر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلزَّقُّومِ", "translit": "ِmwُّqَّzlٱ", "root": "زقم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 63, "text": "إِنَّا جَعَلْنَٰهَا فِتْنَةً لِّلظَّٰلِمِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed, We have made it a torment for the wrongdoers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جَعَلْنَٰهَا", "translit": "āَhَٰnْlَʿعَjg", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِتْنَةً", "translit": "ًẗَnْtِf", "root": "فتن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لِّلظَّٰلِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِlَّٰẓlِّl", "root": "ظلم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 64, "text": "إِنَّهَا شَجَرَةٌ تَخْرُجُ فِىٓ أَصْلِ ٱلْجَحِيمِ ", "translation": "Indeed, it is a tree issuing from the bottom of the Hellfire,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّهَا", "translit": "āَhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "شَجَرَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَrَjgَhs", "root": "شجر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تَخْرُجُ", "translit": "ُjgُrْhkَt", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَصْلِ", "translit": "ِlْṣَaʾ", "root": "اصل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْجَحِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِḥَjgْlٱ", "root": "جحم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 65, "text": "طَلْعُهَا كَأَنَّهُۥ رُءُوسُ ٱلشَّيَٰطِينِ ", "translation": "Its emerging fruit as if it was heads of the devils.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "طَلْعُهَا", "translit": "āَhُʿعْlَṭ", "root": "طلع"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَأَنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnَaʾَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رُءُوسُ", "translit": "ُswُءُr", "root": "راس"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلشَّيَٰطِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِṭَٰyَّhslٱ", "root": "شطن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 66, "text": "فَإِنَّهُمْ لَءَاكِلُونَ مِنْهَا فَمَالِـُٔونَ مِنْهَا ٱلْبُطُونَ ", "translation": "And indeed, they will eat from it and fill with it their bellies.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَإِنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَءَاكِلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlِkāَءَl", "root": "اكل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِنْهَا", "translit": "āَhْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَمَالِـُٔونَ", "translit": "َnwُٔـِlāَmَf", "root": "ملا"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِنْهَا", "translit": "āَhْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْبُطُونَ", "translit": "َnwُṭُbْlٱ", "root": "بطن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 67, "text": "ثُمَّ إِنَّ لَهُمْ عَلَيْهَا لَشَوْبًا مِّنْ حَمِيمٍ ", "translation": "Then indeed, they will have after it a mixture of scalding water.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَلَيْهَا", "translit": "āَhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَشَوْبًا", "translit": "āًbْwَhsَl", "root": "شوب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "حَمِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِmَḥ", "root": "حمم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 68, "text": "ثُمَّ إِنَّ مَرْجِعَهُمْ لَإِلَى ٱلْجَحِيمِ ", "translation": "Then indeed, their return will be to the Hellfire.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَرْجِعَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَʿعِjgْrَm", "root": "رجع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَإِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْجَحِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِḥَjgْlٱ", "root": "جحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 69, "text": "إِنَّهُمْ أَلْفَوْا۟ ءَابَآءَهُمْ ضَآلِّينَ ", "translation": "Indeed they found their fathers astray.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَلْفَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَfْlَaʾ", "root": "لفو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَابَآءَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَءٓāَbāَء", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ضَآلِّينَ", "translit": "َnyِّlٓāَḍ", "root": "ضلل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 70, "text": "فَهُمْ عَلَىٰٓ ءَاثَٰرِهِمْ يُهْرَعُونَ ", "translation": "So they hastened [to follow] in their footsteps.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَاثَٰرِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِrَٰhtāَء", "root": "اثر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يُهْرَعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعَrْhُy", "root": "هرع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 71, "text": "وَلَقَدْ ضَلَّ قَبْلَهُمْ أَكْثَرُ ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ ", "translation": "And there had already strayed before them most of the former peoples,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ضَلَّ", "translit": "َّlَḍ", "root": "ضلل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قَبْلَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَكْثَرُ", "translit": "ُrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَّwَaʾْlٱ", "root": "اول"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 72, "text": "وَلَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا فِيهِم مُّنذِرِينَ ", "translation": "And We had already sent among them warners.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَرْسَلْنَا", "translit": "āَnْlَsْrَaʾ", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِيهِم", "translit": "mِhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مُّنذِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِhdnُّm", "root": "نذر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 73, "text": "فَٱنظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلْمُنذَرِينَ ", "translation": "Then look how was the end of those who were warned -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱنظُرْ", "translit": "ْrُẓnٱَf", "root": "نظر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَيْفَ", "translit": "َfْyَk", "root": "كيف"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَٰقِبَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَbِqَٰʿع", "root": "عقب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمُنذَرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrَhdnُmْlٱ", "root": "نذر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 74, "text": "إِلَّا عِبَادَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلْمُخْلَصِينَ ", "translation": "But not the chosen servants of Allāh.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عِبَادَ", "translit": "َdāَbِʿع", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُخْلَصِينَ", "translit": "َnyِṣَlْhkُmْlٱ", "root": "خلص"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 75, "text": "وَلَقَدْ نَادَىٰنَا نُوحٌ فَلَنِعْمَ ٱلْمُجِيبُونَ ", "translation": "And Noah had certainly called Us, and [We are] the best of responders.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَادَىٰنَا", "translit": "āَnٰàَdāَn", "root": "ندي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نُوحٌ", "translit": "ٌḥwُn", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَلَنِعْمَ", "translit": "َmْʿعِnَlَf", "root": "نعم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمُجِيبُونَ", "translit": "َnwُbyِjgُmْlٱ", "root": "جوب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 76, "text": "وَنَجَّيْنَٰهُ وَأَهْلَهُۥ مِنَ ٱلْكَرْبِ ٱلْعَظِيمِ ", "translation": "And We saved him and his family from the great affliction.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَنَجَّيْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْyَّjgَnَw", "root": "نجو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَأَهْلَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَlْhَaʾَw", "root": "اهل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْكَرْبِ", "translit": "ِbْrَkْlٱ", "root": "كرب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْعَظِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِẓَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عظم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 77, "text": "وَجَعَلْنَا ذُرِّيَّتَهُۥ هُمُ ٱلْبَاقِينَ ", "translation": "And We made his descendants those remaining [on the earth]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَجَعَلْنَا", "translit": "āَnْlَʿعَjgَw", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ذُرِّيَّتَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَtَّyِّrُhd", "root": "ذرر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "هُمُ", "translit": "ُmُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْبَاقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqāَbْlٱ", "root": "بقي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 78, "text": "وَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِى ٱلْءَاخِرِينَ ", "translation": "And left for him [favorable mention] among later generations:", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَتَرَكْنَا", "translit": "āَnْkَrَtَw", "root": "ترك"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 79, "text": "سَلَٰمٌ عَلَىٰ نُوحٍ فِى ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "\"Peace upon Noah among the worlds.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "سَلَٰمٌ", "translit": "ٌmَٰlَs", "root": "سلم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نُوحٍ", "translit": "ٍḥwُn", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 80, "text": "إِنَّا كَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِى ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed, We thus reward the doers of good.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَجْزِى", "translit": "àِzْjgَn", "root": "جزي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِsْḥُmْlٱ", "root": "حسن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 81, "text": "إِنَّهُۥ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed, he was of Our believing servants.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عِبَادِنَا", "translit": "āَnِdāَbِʿع", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُmْlٱ", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 82, "text": "ثُمَّ أَغْرَقْنَا ٱلْءَاخَرِينَ ", "translation": "Then We drowned the others [i.e., disbelievers].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَغْرَقْنَا", "translit": "āَnْqَrْغَaʾ", "root": "غرق"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخَرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrَhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 83, "text": "وَإِنَّ مِن شِيعَتِهِۦ لَإِبْرَٰهِيمَ ", "translation": "And indeed, among his kind was Abraham,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "شِيعَتِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِtَʿعyِhs", "root": "شيع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَإِبْرَٰهِيمَ", "translit": "َmyِhَٰrْbِiʾَl", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 84, "text": "إِذْ جَآءَ رَبَّهُۥ بِقَلْبٍ سَلِيمٍ ", "translation": "When he came to his Lord with a sound heart", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِقَلْبٍ", "translit": "ٍbْlَqِb", "root": "قلب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "سَلِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِlَs", "root": "سلم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 85, "text": "إِذْ قَالَ لِأَبِيهِ وَقَوْمِهِۦ مَاذَا تَعْبُدُونَ ", "translation": "[And] when he said to his father and his people, \"What do you worship?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِأَبِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِbَaʾِl", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَقَوْمِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِmْwَqَw", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَاذَا", "translit": "āَhdāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تَعْبُدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdُbْʿعَt", "root": "عبد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 86, "text": "أَئِفْكًا ءَالِهَةً دُونَ ٱللَّهِ تُرِيدُونَ ", "translation": "Is it falsehood [as] gods other than Allāh you desire?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَئِفْكًا", "translit": "āًkْfِyʾَaʾ", "root": "افك"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ءَالِهَةً", "translit": "ًẗَhِlāَء", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "دُونَ", "translit": "َnwُd", "root": "دون"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تُرِيدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdyِrُt", "root": "رود"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 87, "text": "فَمَا ظَنُّكُم بِرَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "Then what is your thought about the Lord of the worlds?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَمَا", "translit": "āَmَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ظَنُّكُم", "translit": "mُkُّnَẓ", "root": "ظنن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِرَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَrِb", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 88, "text": "فَنَظَرَ نَظْرَةً فِى ٱلنُّجُومِ ", "translation": "And he cast a look at the stars", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَنَظَرَ", "translit": "َrَẓَnَf", "root": "نظر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَظْرَةً", "translit": "ًẗَrْẓَn", "root": "نظر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلنُّجُومِ", "translit": "ِmwُjgُّnlٱ", "root": "نجم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 89, "text": "فَقَالَ إِنِّى سَقِيمٌ ", "translation": "And said, \"Indeed, I am [about to be] ill.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَf", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "سَقِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِqَs", "root": "سقم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 90, "text": "فَتَوَلَّوْا۟ عَنْهُ مُدْبِرِينَ ", "translation": "So they turned away from him, departing.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَتَوَلَّوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَّlَwَtَf", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَنْهُ", "translit": "ُhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مُدْبِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِbْdُm", "root": "دبر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 91, "text": "فَرَاغَ إِلَىٰٓ ءَالِهَتِهِمْ فَقَالَ أَلَا تَأْكُلُونَ ", "translation": "Then he turned to their gods and said, \"Do you not eat?[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَرَاغَ", "translit": "َغāَrَf", "root": "روغ"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَالِهَتِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِtَhِlāَء", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَf", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَلَا", "translit": "āَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تَأْكُلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlُkْaʾَt", "root": "اكل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 92, "text": "مَا لَكُمْ لَا تَنطِقُونَ ", "translation": "What is [wrong] with you that you do not speak?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَنطِقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqِṭnَt", "root": "نطق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 93, "text": "فَرَاغَ عَلَيْهِمْ ضَرْبًۢا بِٱلْيَمِينِ ", "translation": "And he turned upon them a blow with [his] right hand.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَرَاغَ", "translit": "َغāَrَf", "root": "روغ"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ضَرْبًۢا", "translit": "āًۢbْrَḍ", "root": "ضرب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِٱلْيَمِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِmَyْlٱِb", "root": "يمن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 94, "text": "فَأَقْبَلُوٓا۟ إِلَيْهِ يَزِفُّونَ ", "translation": "Then they [i.e., the people] came toward him, hastening.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَقْبَلُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlَbْqَaʾَf", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَزِفُّونَ", "translit": "َnwُّfِzَy", "root": "زفف"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 95, "text": "قَالَ أَتَعْبُدُونَ مَا تَنْحِتُونَ ", "translation": "He said, \"Do you worship that which you [yourselves] carve,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَتَعْبُدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdُbْʿعَtَaʾ", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَنْحِتُونَ", "translit": "َnwُtِḥْnَt", "root": "نحت"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 96, "text": "وَٱللَّهُ خَلَقَكُمْ وَمَا تَعْمَلُونَ ", "translation": "While Allāh created you and that which you do?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "خَلَقَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَqَlَhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَعْمَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَmْʿعَt", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 97, "text": "قَالُوا۟ ٱبْنُوا۟ لَهُۥ بُنْيَٰنًا فَأَلْقُوهُ فِى ٱلْجَحِيمِ ", "translation": "They said, \"Construct for him a structure [i.e., furnace] and throw him into the burning fire.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱبْنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnْbٱ", "root": "بني"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بُنْيَٰنًا", "translit": "āًnَٰyْnُb", "root": "بني"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَأَلْقُوهُ", "translit": "ُhwُqْlَaʾَf", "root": "لقي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْجَحِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِḥَjgْlٱ", "root": "جحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 98, "text": "فَأَرَادُوا۟ بِهِۦ كَيْدًا فَجَعَلْنَٰهُمُ ٱلْأَسْفَلِينَ ", "translation": "And they intended for him a plan [i.e., harm], but We made them the most debased.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَرَادُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُdāَrَaʾَf", "root": "رود"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَيْدًا", "translit": "āًdْyَk", "root": "كيد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَجَعَلْنَٰهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhَٰnْlَʿعَjgَf", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْأَسْفَلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَfْsَaʾْlٱ", "root": "سفل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 99, "text": "وَقَالَ إِنِّى ذَاهِبٌ إِلَىٰ رَبِّى سَيَهْدِينِ ", "translation": "And [then] he said, \"Indeed, I will go to [where I am ordered by] my Lord; He will guide me.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ذَاهِبٌ", "translit": "ٌbِhāَhd", "root": "ذهب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "رَبِّى", "translit": "àِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "سَيَهْدِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِdْhَyَs", "root": "هدي"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 100, "text": "رَبِّ هَبْ لِى مِنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ", "translation": "My Lord, grant me [a child] from among the righteous.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هَبْ", "translit": "ْbَh", "root": "وهب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِى", "translit": "àِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ", "translit": "َnyِḥِlَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صلح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 101, "text": "فَبَشَّرْنَٰهُ بِغُلَٰمٍ حَلِيمٍ ", "translation": "So We gave him good tidings of a forbearing boy.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَبَشَّرْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْrَّhsَbَf", "root": "بشر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِغُلَٰمٍ", "translit": "ٍmَٰlُغِb", "root": "غلم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حَلِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِlَḥ", "root": "حلم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 102, "text": "فَلَمَّا بَلَغَ مَعَهُ ٱلسَّعْىَ قَالَ يَٰبُنَىَّ إِنِّىٓ أَرَىٰ فِى ٱلْمَنَامِ أَنِّىٓ أَذْبَحُكَ فَٱنظُرْ مَاذَا تَرَىٰۚ قَالَ يَٰٓأَبَتِ ٱفْعَلْ مَا تُؤْمَرُۖ سَتَجِدُنِىٓ إِن شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ ", "translation": "And when he reached with him [the age of] exertion,[1] he said, \"O my son, indeed I have seen in a dream that I [must] sacrifice you, so see what you think.\" He said, \"O my father, do as you are commanded. You will find me, if Allāh wills, of the steadfast.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَلَغَ", "translit": "َغَlَb", "root": "بلغ"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَعَهُ", "translit": "ُhَʿعَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلسَّعْىَ", "translit": "َàْʿعَّslٱ", "root": "سعي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَٰبُنَىَّ", "translit": "َّàَnُbَٰy", "root": "بني"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِنِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَرَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَrَaʾ", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلْمَنَامِ", "translit": "ِmāَnَmْlٱ", "root": "نوم"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَنِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَذْبَحُكَ", "translit": "َkُḥَbْhdَaʾ", "root": "ذبح"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "فَٱنظُرْ", "translit": "ْrُẓnٱَf", "root": "نظر"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مَاذَا", "translit": "āَhdāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "تَرَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَrَt", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَبَتِ", "translit": "ِtَbَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱفْعَلْ", "translit": "ْlَʿعْfٱ", "root": "فعل"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "تُؤْمَرُ", "translit": "ُrَmْwʾُt", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "سَتَجِدُنِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِnُdِjgَtَs", "root": "وجد"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "شَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِbَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صبر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 103, "text": "فَلَمَّآ أَسْلَمَا وَتَلَّهُۥ لِلْجَبِينِ ", "translation": "And when they had both submitted[1] and he put him down upon his forehead,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَمَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَسْلَمَا", "translit": "āَmَlْsَaʾ", "root": "سلم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَتَلَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّlَtَw", "root": "تلل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لِلْجَبِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِbَjgْlِl", "root": "جبن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 104, "text": "وَنَٰدَيْنَٰهُ أَن يَٰٓإِبْرَٰهِيمُ ", "translation": "We called to him, \"O Abraham,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَنَٰدَيْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْyَdَٰnَw", "root": "ندي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَٰٓإِبْرَٰهِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِhَٰrْbِiʾَٰٓy", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 105, "text": "قَدْ صَدَّقْتَ ٱلرُّءْيَآۚ إِنَّا كَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِى ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ ", "translation": "You have fulfilled the vision.\" Indeed, We thus reward the doers of good.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَدْ", "translit": "ْdَq", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "صَدَّقْتَ", "translit": "َtْqَّdَṣ", "root": "صدق"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلرُّءْيَآ", "translit": "ٓāَyْءُّrlٱ", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "نَجْزِى", "translit": "àِzْjgَn", "root": "جزي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِsْḥُmْlٱ", "root": "حسن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 106, "text": "إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَهُوَ ٱلْبَلَٰٓؤُا۟ ٱلْمُبِينُ ", "translation": "Indeed, this was the clear trial.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْبَلَٰٓؤُا۟", "translit": "۟āُwʾَٰٓlَbْlٱ", "root": "بلو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمُبِينُ", "translit": "ُnyِbُmْlٱ", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 107, "text": "وَفَدَيْنَٰهُ بِذِبْحٍ عَظِيمٍ ", "translation": "And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَفَدَيْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْyَdَfَw", "root": "فدي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِذِبْحٍ", "translit": "ٍḥْbِhdِb", "root": "ذبح"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَظِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِẓَʿع", "root": "عظم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 108, "text": "وَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِى ٱلْءَاخِرِينَ ", "translation": "And We left for him [favorable mention] among later generations:", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَتَرَكْنَا", "translit": "āَnْkَrَtَw", "root": "ترك"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 109, "text": "سَلَٰمٌ عَلَىٰٓ إِبْرَٰهِيمَ ", "translation": "\"Peace upon Abraham.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "سَلَٰمٌ", "translit": "ٌmَٰlَs", "root": "سلم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِبْرَٰهِيمَ", "translit": "َmyِhَٰrْbِiʾ", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 110, "text": "كَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِى ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed, We thus reward the doers of good.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَجْزِى", "translit": "àِzْjgَn", "root": "جزي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِsْḥُmْlٱ", "root": "حسن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 111, "text": "إِنَّهُۥ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed, he was of Our believing servants.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عِبَادِنَا", "translit": "āَnِdāَbِʿع", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُmْlٱ", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 112, "text": "وَبَشَّرْنَٰهُ بِإِسْحَٰقَ نَبِيًّا مِّنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ", "translation": "And We gave him good tidings of Isaac, a prophet from among the righteous.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَبَشَّرْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْrَّhsَbَw", "root": "بشر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِإِسْحَٰقَ", "translit": "َqَٰḥْsِiʾِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَبِيًّا", "translit": "āًّyِbَn", "root": "نبا"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ", "translit": "َnyِḥِlَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صلح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 113, "text": "وَبَٰرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ وَعَلَىٰٓ إِسْحَٰقَۚ وَمِن ذُرِّيَّتِهِمَا مُحْسِنٌ وَظَالِمٌ لِّنَفْسِهِۦ مُبِينٌ ", "translation": "And We blessed him and Isaac. But among their descendants is the doer of good and the clearly unjust to himself [i.e., sinner].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَبَٰرَكْنَا", "translit": "āَnْkَrَٰbَw", "root": "برك"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَعَلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlَʿعَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِسْحَٰقَ", "translit": "َqَٰḥْsِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَمِن", "translit": "nِmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ذُرِّيَّتِهِمَا", "translit": "āَmِhِtَّyِّrُhd", "root": "ذرر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مُحْسِنٌ", "translit": "ٌnِsْḥُm", "root": "حسن"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَظَالِمٌ", "translit": "ٌmِlāَẓَw", "root": "ظلم"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لِّنَفْسِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِsْfَnِّl", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مُبِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِbُm", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 114, "text": "وَلَقَدْ مَنَنَّا عَلَىٰ مُوسَىٰ وَهَٰرُونَ ", "translation": "And We did certainly confer favor upon Moses and Aaron.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَنَنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَnَm", "root": "منن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مُوسَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَswُm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَهَٰرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrَٰhَw", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 115, "text": "وَنَجَّيْنَٰهُمَا وَقَوْمَهُمَا مِنَ ٱلْكَرْبِ ٱلْعَظِيمِ ", "translation": "And We saved them and their people from the great affliction,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَنَجَّيْنَٰهُمَا", "translit": "āَmُhَٰnْyَّjgَnَw", "root": "نجو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَقَوْمَهُمَا", "translit": "āَmُhَmْwَqَw", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْكَرْبِ", "translit": "ِbْrَkْlٱ", "root": "كرب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْعَظِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِẓَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عظم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 116, "text": "وَنَصَرْنَٰهُمْ فَكَانُوا۟ هُمُ ٱلْغَٰلِبِينَ ", "translation": "And We supported them so it was they who overcame.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَنَصَرْنَٰهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَٰnْrَṣَnَw", "root": "نصر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَكَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَkَf", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "هُمُ", "translit": "ُmُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْغَٰلِبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbِlَٰغْlٱ", "root": "غلب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 117, "text": "وَءَاتَيْنَٰهُمَا ٱلْكِتَٰبَ ٱلْمُسْتَبِينَ ", "translation": "And We gave them the explicit Scripture [i.e., the Torah],", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَءَاتَيْنَٰهُمَا", "translit": "āَmُhَٰnْyَtāَءَw", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْكِتَٰبَ", "translit": "َbَٰtِkْlٱ", "root": "كتب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمُسْتَبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbَtْsُmْlٱ", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 118, "text": "وَهَدَيْنَٰهُمَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ ", "translation": "And We guided them on the straight path.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَهَدَيْنَٰهُمَا", "translit": "āَmُhَٰnْyَdَhَw", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلصِّرَٰطَ", "translit": "َṭَٰrِّṣlٱ", "root": "صرط"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ", "translit": "َmyِqَtْsُmْlٱ", "root": "قوم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 119, "text": "وَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِمَا فِى ٱلْءَاخِرِينَ ", "translation": "And We left for them [favorable mention] among later generations:", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَتَرَكْنَا", "translit": "āَnْkَrَtَw", "root": "ترك"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمَا", "translit": "āَmِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 120, "text": "سَلَٰمٌ عَلَىٰ مُوسَىٰ وَهَٰرُونَ ", "translation": "\"Peace upon Moses and Aaron.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "سَلَٰمٌ", "translit": "ٌmَٰlَs", "root": "سلم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مُوسَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَswُm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَهَٰرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrَٰhَw", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 121, "text": "إِنَّا كَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِى ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed, We thus reward the doers of good.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَجْزِى", "translit": "àِzْjgَn", "root": "جزي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِsْḥُmْlٱ", "root": "حسن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 122, "text": "إِنَّهُمَا مِنْ عِبَادِنَا ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed, they were of Our believing servants.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّهُمَا", "translit": "āَmُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عِبَادِنَا", "translit": "āَnِdāَbِʿع", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُmْlٱ", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 123, "text": "وَإِنَّ إِلْيَاسَ لَمِنَ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ ", "translation": "And indeed, Elias was from among the messengers,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِلْيَاسَ", "translit": "َsāَyْlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَمِنَ", "translit": "َnِmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَsْrُmْlٱ", "root": "رسل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 124, "text": "إِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهِۦٓ أَلَا تَتَّقُونَ ", "translation": "When he said to his people, \"Will you not fear Allāh?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِقَوْمِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِmْwَqِl", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَلَا", "translit": "āَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَتَّقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqَّtَt", "root": "وقي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 125, "text": "أَتَدْعُونَ بَعْلًا وَتَذَرُونَ أَحْسَنَ ٱلْخَٰلِقِينَ ", "translation": "Do you call upon Baʿl[1] and leave the best of creators -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَتَدْعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعْdَtَaʾ", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَعْلًا", "translit": "āًlْʿعَb", "root": "بعل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَتَذَرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrَhdَtَw", "root": "وذر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَحْسَنَ", "translit": "َnَsْḥَaʾ", "root": "حسن"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْخَٰلِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِlَٰhkْlٱ", "root": "خلق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 126, "text": "ٱللَّهَ رَبَّكُمْ وَرَبَّ ءَابَآئِكُمُ ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ ", "translation": "Allāh, your Lord and the Lord of your first forefathers?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَرَبَّ", "translit": "َّbَrَw", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ءَابَآئِكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkِyʾٓāَbāَء", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَّwَaʾْlٱ", "root": "اول"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 127, "text": "فَكَذَّبُوهُ فَإِنَّهُمْ لَمُحْضَرُونَ ", "translation": "And they denied him, so indeed, they will be brought [for punishment],", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَكَذَّبُوهُ", "translit": "ُhwُbَّhdَkَf", "root": "كذب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَإِنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَمُحْضَرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrَḍْḥُmَl", "root": "حضر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 128, "text": "إِلَّا عِبَادَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلْمُخْلَصِينَ ", "translation": "Except the chosen servants of Allāh.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عِبَادَ", "translit": "َdāَbِʿع", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُخْلَصِينَ", "translit": "َnyِṣَlْhkُmْlٱ", "root": "خلص"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 129, "text": "وَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِى ٱلْءَاخِرِينَ ", "translation": "And We left for him [favorable mention] among later generations:", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَتَرَكْنَا", "translit": "āَnْkَrَtَw", "root": "ترك"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 130, "text": "سَلَٰمٌ عَلَىٰٓ إِلْ يَاسِينَ ", "translation": "\"Peace upon Elias.\"[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "سَلَٰمٌ", "translit": "ٌmَٰlَs", "root": "سلم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلْ يَاسِينَ", "translit": "َnyِsāَylِiʾ", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 131, "text": "إِنَّا كَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِى ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed, We thus reward the doers of good.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَجْزِى", "translit": "àِzْjgَn", "root": "جزي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِsْḥُmْlٱ", "root": "حسن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 132, "text": "إِنَّهُۥ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed, he was of Our believing servants.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عِبَادِنَا", "translit": "āَnِdāَbِʿع", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُmْlٱ", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 133, "text": "وَإِنَّ لُوطًا لَّمِنَ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ ", "translation": "And indeed, Lot was among the messengers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لُوطًا", "translit": "āًṭwُl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَّمِنَ", "translit": "َnِmَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَsْrُmْlٱ", "root": "رسل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 134, "text": "إِذْ نَجَّيْنَٰهُ وَأَهْلَهُۥٓ أَجْمَعِينَ ", "translation": "[So mention] when We saved him and his family, all,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَجَّيْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْyَّjgَn", "root": "نجو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَأَهْلَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَlْhَaʾَw", "root": "اهل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَجْمَعِينَ", "translit": "َnyِʿعَmْjgَaʾ", "root": "جمع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 135, "text": "إِلَّا عَجُوزًا فِى ٱلْغَٰبِرِينَ ", "translation": "Except an old woman [i.e., his wife] among those who remained [with the evildoers].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَجُوزًا", "translit": "āًzwُjgَʿع", "root": "عجز"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْغَٰبِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِbَٰغْlٱ", "root": "غبر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 136, "text": "ثُمَّ دَمَّرْنَا ٱلْءَاخَرِينَ ", "translation": "Then We destroyed the others.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "دَمَّرْنَا", "translit": "āَnْrَّmَd", "root": "دمر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخَرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrَhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 137, "text": "وَإِنَّكُمْ لَتَمُرُّونَ عَلَيْهِم مُّصْبِحِينَ ", "translation": "And indeed, you pass by them in the morning", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَتَمُرُّونَ", "translit": "َnwُّrُmَtَl", "root": "مرر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِم", "translit": "mِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مُّصْبِحِينَ", "translit": "َnyِḥِbْṣُّm", "root": "صبح"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 138, "text": "وَبِٱلَّيْلِۗ أَفَلَا تَعْقِلُونَ ", "translation": "And at night. Then will you not use reason?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَبِٱلَّيْلِ", "translit": "ِlْyَّlٱِbَw", "root": "ليل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَفَلَا", "translit": "āَlَfَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تَعْقِلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlِqْʿعَt", "root": "عقل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 139, "text": "وَإِنَّ يُونُسَ لَمِنَ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ ", "translation": "And indeed, Jonah was among the messengers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يُونُسَ", "translit": "َsُnwُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَمِنَ", "translit": "َnِmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَsْrُmْlٱ", "root": "رسل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 140, "text": "إِذْ أَبَقَ إِلَى ٱلْفُلْكِ ٱلْمَشْحُونِ ", "translation": "[Mention] when he ran away to the laden ship.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَبَقَ", "translit": "َqَbَaʾ", "root": "ابق"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْفُلْكِ", "translit": "ِkْlُfْlٱ", "root": "فلك"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمَشْحُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُḥْhsَmْlٱ", "root": "شحن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 141, "text": "فَسَاهَمَ فَكَانَ مِنَ ٱلْمُدْحَضِينَ ", "translation": "And he drew lots[1] and was among the losers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَسَاهَمَ", "translit": "َmَhāَsَf", "root": "سهم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَكَانَ", "translit": "َnāَkَf", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُدْحَضِينَ", "translit": "َnyِḍَḥْdُmْlٱ", "root": "دحض"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 142, "text": "فَٱلْتَقَمَهُ ٱلْحُوتُ وَهُوَ مُلِيمٌ ", "translation": "Then the fish swallowed him, while he was blameworthy.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱلْتَقَمَهُ", "translit": "ُhَmَqَtْlٱَf", "root": "لقم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْحُوتُ", "translit": "ُtwُḥْlٱ", "root": "حوت"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مُلِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِlُm", "root": "لوم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 143, "text": "فَلَوْلَآ أَنَّهُۥ كَانَ مِنَ ٱلْمُسَبِّحِينَ ", "translation": "And had he not been of those who exalt Allāh,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَوْلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlْwَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمُسَبِّحِينَ", "translit": "َnyِḥِّbَsُmْlٱ", "root": "سبح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 144, "text": "لَلَبِثَ فِى بَطْنِهِۦٓ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُونَ ", "translation": "He would have remained inside its belly until the Day they are resurrected.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَلَبِثَ", "translit": "َhtِbَlَl", "root": "لبث"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بَطْنِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِnْṭَb", "root": "بطن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَوْمِ", "translit": "ِmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يُبْعَثُونَ", "translit": "َnwُhtَʿعْbُy", "root": "بعث"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 145, "text": "فَنَبَذْنَٰهُ بِٱلْعَرَآءِ وَهُوَ سَقِيمٌ ", "translation": "But We threw him onto the open shore while he was ill.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَنَبَذْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْhdَbَnَf", "root": "نبذ"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِٱلْعَرَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَrَʿعْlٱِb", "root": "عري"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "سَقِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِqَs", "root": "سقم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 146, "text": "وَأَنۢبَتْنَا عَلَيْهِ شَجَرَةً مِّن يَقْطِينٍ ", "translation": "And We caused to grow over him a gourd vine.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنۢبَتْنَا", "translit": "āَnْtَbۢnَaʾَw", "root": "نبت"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "شَجَرَةً", "translit": "ًẗَrَjgَhs", "root": "شجر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَقْطِينٍ", "translit": "ٍnyِṭْqَy", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 147, "text": "وَأَرْسَلْنَٰهُ إِلَىٰ مِا۟ئَةِ أَلْفٍ أَوْ يَزِيدُونَ ", "translation": "And We sent him[1] to [his people of] a hundred thousand or more.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَرْسَلْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْlَsْrَaʾَw", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِا۟ئَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَyʾ۟āِm", "root": "ماي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَلْفٍ", "translit": "ٍfْlَaʾ", "root": "الف"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَزِيدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdyِzَy", "root": "زيد"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 148, "text": "فَـَٔامَنُوا۟ فَمَتَّعْنَٰهُمْ إِلَىٰ حِينٍ ", "translation": "And they believed, so We gave them enjoyment [of life] for a time.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَـَٔامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَٔـَf", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَمَتَّعْنَٰهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَٰnْʿعَّtَmَf", "root": "متع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "حِينٍ", "translit": "ٍnyِḥ", "root": "حين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 149, "text": "فَٱسْتَفْتِهِمْ أَلِرَبِّكَ ٱلْبَنَاتُ وَلَهُمُ ٱلْبَنُونَ ", "translation": "So inquire of them, [O Muḥammad], \"Does your Lord have daughters while they have sons?[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱسْتَفْتِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِtْfَtْsٱَf", "root": "فتي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَلِرَبِّكَ", "translit": "َkِّbَrِlَaʾ", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْبَنَاتُ", "translit": "ُtāَnَbْlٱ", "root": "بني"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَلَهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْبَنُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnَbْlٱ", "root": "بني"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 150, "text": "أَمْ خَلَقْنَا ٱلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةَ إِنَٰثًا وَهُمْ شَٰهِدُونَ ", "translation": "Or did We create the angels as females while they were witnesses?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "خَلَقْنَا", "translit": "āَnْqَlَhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةَ", "translit": "َẗَkِyʾَٰٓlَmْlٱ", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِنَٰثًا", "translit": "āًhtَٰnِiʾ", "root": "انث"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "شَٰهِدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdِhَٰhs", "root": "شهد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 151, "text": "أَلَآ إِنَّهُم مِّنْ إِفْكِهِمْ لَيَقُولُونَ ", "translation": "Unquestionably, it is out of their [invented] falsehood that they say,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّهُم", "translit": "mُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِفْكِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِkْfِiʾ", "root": "افك"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَيَقُولُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlwُqَyَl", "root": "قول"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 152, "text": "وَلَدَ ٱللَّهُ وَإِنَّهُمْ لَكَٰذِبُونَ ", "translation": "\"Allāh has begotten,\" and indeed, they are liars.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَدَ", "translit": "َdَlَw", "root": "ولد"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَإِنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَكَٰذِبُونَ", "translit": "َnwُbِhdَٰkَl", "root": "كذب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 153, "text": "أَصْطَفَى ٱلْبَنَاتِ عَلَى ٱلْبَنِينَ ", "translation": "Has He chosen daughters over sons?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَصْطَفَى", "translit": "àَfَṭْṣَaʾ", "root": "صفو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْبَنَاتِ", "translit": "ِtāَnَbْlٱ", "root": "بني"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَى", "translit": "àَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْبَنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnَbْlٱ", "root": "بني"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 154, "text": "مَا لَكُمْ كَيْفَ تَحْكُمُونَ ", "translation": "What is [wrong] with you? How do you make judgement?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَيْفَ", "translit": "َfْyَk", "root": "كيف"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَحْكُمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmُkْḥَt", "root": "حكم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 155, "text": "أَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُونَ ", "translation": "Then will you not be reminded?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَفَلَا", "translit": "āَlَfَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَذَكَّرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrَّkَhdَt", "root": "ذكر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 156, "text": "أَمْ لَكُمْ سُلْطَٰنٌ مُّبِينٌ ", "translation": "Or do you have a clear authority?[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "سُلْطَٰنٌ", "translit": "ٌnَٰṭْlُs", "root": "سلط"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مُّبِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِbُّm", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 157, "text": "فَأْتُوا۟ بِكِتَٰبِكُمْ إِن كُنتُمْ صَٰدِقِينَ ", "translation": "Then produce your scripture, if you should be truthful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأْتُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُtْaʾَf", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِكِتَٰبِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِbَٰtِkِb", "root": "كتب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كُنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "صَٰدِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِdَٰṣ", "root": "صدق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 158, "text": "وَجَعَلُوا۟ بَيْنَهُۥ وَبَيْنَ ٱلْجِنَّةِ نَسَبًاۚ وَلَقَدْ عَلِمَتِ ٱلْجِنَّةُ إِنَّهُمْ لَمُحْضَرُونَ ", "translation": "And they have made [i.e., claimed] between Him and the jinn a lineage, but the jinn have already known that they [who made such claims] will be brought [to punishment].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَجَعَلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlَʿعَjgَw", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَيْنَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَبَيْنَ", "translit": "َnْyَbَw", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْجِنَّةِ", "translit": "ِẗَّnِjgْlٱ", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "نَسَبًا", "translit": "āًbَsَn", "root": "نسب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَلَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "عَلِمَتِ", "translit": "ِtَmِlَʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْجِنَّةُ", "translit": "ُẗَّnِjgْlٱ", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "إِنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لَمُحْضَرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrَḍْḥُmَl", "root": "حضر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 159, "text": "سُبْحَٰنَ ٱللَّهِ عَمَّا يَصِفُونَ ", "translation": "Exalted is Allāh above what they describe,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "سُبْحَٰنَ", "translit": "َnَٰḥْbُs", "root": "سبح"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَصِفُونَ", "translit": "َnwُfِṣَy", "root": "وصف"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 160, "text": "إِلَّا عِبَادَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلْمُخْلَصِينَ ", "translation": "Except the chosen servants of Allāh [who do not share in that sin].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عِبَادَ", "translit": "َdāَbِʿع", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُخْلَصِينَ", "translit": "َnyِṣَlْhkُmْlٱ", "root": "خلص"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 161, "text": "فَإِنَّكُمْ وَمَا تَعْبُدُونَ ", "translation": "So indeed, you [disbelievers] and whatever you worship,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَإِنَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّnِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تَعْبُدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdُbْʿعَt", "root": "عبد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 162, "text": "مَآ أَنتُمْ عَلَيْهِ بِفَٰتِنِينَ ", "translation": "You cannot tempt [anyone] away from Him", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِفَٰتِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِtَٰfِb", "root": "فتن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 163, "text": "إِلَّا مَنْ هُوَ صَالِ ٱلْجَحِيمِ ", "translation": "Except he who is to [enter and] burn in the Hellfire.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَنْ", "translit": "ْnَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "صَالِ", "translit": "ِlāَṣ", "root": "صلي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْجَحِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِḥَjgْlٱ", "root": "جحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 164, "text": "وَمَا مِنَّآ إِلَّا لَهُۥ مَقَامٌ مَّعْلُومٌ ", "translation": "[The angels say],[1] \"There is not among us any except that he has a known position.[2]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِنَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَقَامٌ", "translit": "ٌmāَqَm", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مَّعْلُومٌ", "translit": "ٌmwُlْʿعَّm", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 165, "text": "وَإِنَّا لَنَحْنُ ٱلصَّآفُّونَ ", "translation": "And indeed, we are those who line up [for prayer].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَنَحْنُ", "translit": "ُnْḥَnَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلصَّآفُّونَ", "translit": "َnwُّfٓāَّṣlٱ", "root": "صفف"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 166, "text": "وَإِنَّا لَنَحْنُ ٱلْمُسَبِّحُونَ ", "translation": "And indeed, we are those who exalt Allāh.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَنَحْنُ", "translit": "ُnْḥَnَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمُسَبِّحُونَ", "translit": "َnwُḥِّbَsُmْlٱ", "root": "سبح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 167, "text": "وَإِن كَانُوا۟ لَيَقُولُونَ ", "translation": "And indeed, they [i.e., the disbelievers] used to say,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِن", "translit": "nِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَيَقُولُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlwُqَyَl", "root": "قول"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 168, "text": "لَوْ أَنَّ عِندَنَا ذِكْرًا مِّنَ ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ ", "translation": "\"If we had a message from [those of] the former peoples,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَوْ", "translit": "ْwَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عِندَنَا", "translit": "āَnَdnِʿع", "root": "عند"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ذِكْرًا", "translit": "āًrْkِhd", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَّwَaʾْlٱ", "root": "اول"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 169, "text": "لَكُنَّا عِبَادَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلْمُخْلَصِينَ ", "translation": "We would have been the chosen servants of Allāh.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَكُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُkَl", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عِبَادَ", "translit": "َdāَbِʿع", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُخْلَصِينَ", "translit": "َnyِṣَlْhkُmْlٱ", "root": "خلص"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 170, "text": "فَكَفَرُوا۟ بِهِۦۖ فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُونَ ", "translation": "But they disbelieved in it,[1] so they are going to know.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَكَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَkَf", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَسَوْفَ", "translit": "َfْwَsَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 171, "text": "وَلَقَدْ سَبَقَتْ كَلِمَتُنَا لِعِبَادِنَا ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ ", "translation": "And Our word [i.e., decree] has already preceded for Our servants, the messengers,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "سَبَقَتْ", "translit": "ْtَqَbَs", "root": "سبق"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَلِمَتُنَا", "translit": "āَnُtَmِlَk", "root": "كلم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لِعِبَادِنَا", "translit": "āَnِdāَbِʿعِl", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَsْrُmْlٱ", "root": "رسل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 172, "text": "إِنَّهُمْ لَهُمُ ٱلْمَنصُورُونَ ", "translation": "[That] indeed, they would be those given victory", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمَنصُورُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrwُṣnَmْlٱ", "root": "نصر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 173, "text": "وَإِنَّ جُندَنَا لَهُمُ ٱلْغَٰلِبُونَ ", "translation": "And [that] indeed, Our soldiers [i.e., the believers] will be those who overcome.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جُندَنَا", "translit": "āَnَdnُjg", "root": "جند"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْغَٰلِبُونَ", "translit": "َnwُbِlَٰغْlٱ", "root": "غلب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 174, "text": "فَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ حَتَّىٰ حِينٍ ", "translation": "So, [O Muḥammad], leave them for a time.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَتَوَلَّ", "translit": "َّlَwَtَf", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَنْهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "حِينٍ", "translit": "ٍnyِḥ", "root": "حين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 175, "text": "وَأَبْصِرْهُمْ فَسَوْفَ يُبْصِرُونَ ", "translation": "And see [what will befall] them, for they are going to see.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَبْصِرْهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhْrِṣْbَaʾَw", "root": "بصر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَسَوْفَ", "translit": "َfْwَsَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يُبْصِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِṣْbُy", "root": "بصر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 176, "text": "أَفَبِعَذَابِنَا يَسْتَعْجِلُونَ ", "translation": "Then for Our punishment are they impatient?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَفَبِعَذَابِنَا", "translit": "āَnِbāَhdَʿعِbَfَaʾ", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَسْتَعْجِلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlِjgْʿعَtْsَy", "root": "عجل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 177, "text": "فَإِذَا نَزَلَ بِسَاحَتِهِمْ فَسَآءَ صَبَاحُ ٱلْمُنذَرِينَ ", "translation": "But when it descends in their territory, then evil is the morning of those who were warned.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَزَلَ", "translit": "َlَzَn", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِسَاحَتِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِtَḥāَsِb", "root": "سوح"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَسَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَsَf", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "صَبَاحُ", "translit": "ُḥāَbَṣ", "root": "صبح"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْمُنذَرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrَhdnُmْlٱ", "root": "نذر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 178, "text": "وَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ حَتَّىٰ حِينٍ ", "translation": "And leave them for a time.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَتَوَلَّ", "translit": "َّlَwَtَw", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَنْهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "حِينٍ", "translit": "ٍnyِḥ", "root": "حين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 179, "text": "وَأَبْصِرْ فَسَوْفَ يُبْصِرُونَ ", "translation": "And see, for they are going to see.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَبْصِرْ", "translit": "ْrِṣْbَaʾَw", "root": "بصر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَسَوْفَ", "translit": "َfْwَsَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يُبْصِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِṣْbُy", "root": "بصر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 180, "text": "سُبْحَٰنَ رَبِّكَ رَبِّ ٱلْعِزَّةِ عَمَّا يَصِفُونَ ", "translation": "Exalted is your Lord, the Lord of might, above what they describe.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "سُبْحَٰنَ", "translit": "َnَٰḥْbُs", "root": "سبح"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبِّكَ", "translit": "َkِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعِزَّةِ", "translit": "ِẗَّzِʿعْlٱ", "root": "عزز"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَصِفُونَ", "translit": "َnwُfِṣَy", "root": "وصف"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 181, "text": "وَسَلَٰمٌ عَلَى ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ ", "translation": "And peace upon the messengers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَسَلَٰمٌ", "translit": "ٌmَٰlَsَw", "root": "سلم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَى", "translit": "àَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَsْrُmْlٱ", "root": "رسل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 182, "text": "وَٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "And praise to Allāh, Lord of the worlds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلْحَمْدُ", "translit": "ُdْmَḥْlٱَw", "root": "حمد"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِl", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": true}], "tafsir": {"6": [{"arabic": "وأما الحكمة في سائر الكواكب السيارة منها والثوابت فخفية لا يطلع عليها كافة الخلق والقدر الذي يحتمله فهم الخلق انها زينة للسماء لتستلذ العين بالنظر اليها وأشار اليه قوله تعالى: ﴿ إنا زينا السماء الدنيا بزينة الكواكب ﴾ {} فجميع اجزاء العالم سماؤه وكواكبه ورياحه وبحاره وجباله ومعادنه ونباته وحيواناته وأعضاء حيواناته لا تخلو ذرة من ذراته عن حكم كثيرة من حكمة واحدة الى عشرة الى الف الى عشرة آلاف وكذا أعضاء الحيوان تنقسم الا ما يعرف حكمتها كالعلم بأن العين للإبصار لا للبطش واليد للبطش لا للمشي والرجل ", "english": "As for the wisdom (hikmah) in the rest of the planets, both the moving (sayyarah) and the fixed (thawabit), it is hidden (khafiyyah) and not accessible to all of creation. The extent that the understanding of creation can bear is that they are an adornment (zīnah) for the sky so that the eye may delight in looking at them, and this is indicated by His saying, the Exalted: 'Indeed, We have adorned the nearest heaven (al-samā' al-dunyā) with an adornment of stars (al-kawākib).' So all parts of the world—its sky, its stars, its winds, its seas, its mountains, its minerals, its plants, its animals, and the limbs of its animals—not a single atom (dharrah) of its atoms is devoid of many wisdoms (ḥikam), from one wisdom to ten, to a thousand, to ten thousand. Likewise, the limbs of the animal are divided except for what is known of their wisdom, such as knowing that the eye is for sight (al-ibṣār) not for striking (al-baṭsh), the hand for striking not for walking (al-mashy), and the foot for walking not for smelling (al-shamm). As for the internal (bāṭinah) limbs—the intestines (al-am'ā'), the gallbladder (al-marārah), the liver (al-kabid), the kidney (al-kulyah), the individual veins (al-'urūq), nerves (al-a'ṣāb), muscles (al-'aḍalāt), and what is in them of cavities (al-tajāwīf), convolutions (al-iltifāf), intertwinings (al-ishtibāk), deviations (al-inḥirāf), fineness (al-daqqah), thickness (al-ghalẓ), and other attributes—the wisdom in them is not known by most people. And those who know them do not know from them except a small amount (qadran yasīran) in addition to what is in the knowledge of Allah, the Exalted: 'And you have not been given of knowledge except a little.'", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Patience and Gratitude", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Patience and Gratitude'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "23": [{"arabic": "ثم تفكر بعد هذه الأهوال فى قول الله تعالى: ﴿ يوم نحشر المتقين إلى الرحمن وفدا ونسوق المجرمين إلى جهنم وردا ﴾ {} وفى قوله تعالى: ﴿ فاهدوهم إلى صراط الجحيم. وقفوهم إنهم مسئولون ﴾ {} فالناس من بعد هذه الأهوال يساقون إلى الصراط وهو جسر ممدود على متن النار أحد من السيف وأدق من الشعر فمن استقام فى هذا العالم على الصراط المستقيم خف على صراط الآخرة ونجا ومن عدل عن الاستقامة فى الدنيا وأثقل ظهره بالأوزار وعصى تعثر فى أول قدم من الصراط وتردى فتفكر الآن فيما يحل من الفزع بفؤادك إذا رأيت الصراط ودقته ثم وقع", "english": "Then reflect after these terrors upon the saying of Allah the Exalted: 'On the Day We gather the righteous to the Most Merciful as a delegation, and drive the criminals to Hell as a thirsty herd' (Quran 19:85-86) and upon His saying: 'So guide them to the path (Siraat) of Hell. And stop them; indeed, they are to be questioned' (Quran 37:23-24). The people after these terrors are driven to the Path (Siraat), which is a bridge extended over the surface of the Fire, sharper than the sword and finer than hair. Whoever was upright (Istiqamah) in this world upon the Straight Path (Siraat al-Mustaqeem) will find the path of the Hereafter light and be saved. And whoever deviated from uprightness (Istiqamah) in the world and burdened his back with sins (Awzar) and disobeyed will stumble at the first step of the Path (Siraat) and fall. So reflect now upon what befalls your heart (Fu'ad) of terror when you see the Path (Siraat) and its fineness, then your sight falls upon the blackness of Hell beneath it, then your hearing is struck by the roaring of the Fire and its rage, and you have been tasked to walk upon the Path (Siraat) with the weakness of your state and the agitation of your heart (Qalb) and the trembling of your foot and the burden of your back with sins (Awzar) that prevent you from walking on the carpet of the earth, let alone the sharpness of the Path (Siraat). How will it be with you when you place one of your feet upon it and feel its sharpness and are compelled to lift the second foot, and the creatures before you slip and stumble, and the guardians of the Fire contend with them with hooks and grappling irons, and you look at them how they are overturned so that their heads descend toward the direction of the Fire and their feet rise. Oh, what a sight, how dreadful it is, and what an ascent, how difficult it is, and what a crossing, how narrow it is. So look at your state as you crawl upon it and ascend to it while you are burdened in the back with your sins (Awzar), turning right and left to the creatures as they tumble into the Fire, and the Messenger, peace be upon him, says: 'O Lord, s'", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Repentance", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter, from 'Book of Repentance'", "badge": "Afterlife"}, {"arabic": "الأصل الخامس: الصراط وهو جسر ممدود على متن جهنم أرق من الشعرة وأحد من السيف قال الله تعالى: ﴿ فاهدوهم إلى صراط الجحيم. وقفوهم إنهم مسئولون ﴾ { سورة الصافات: 23، 24 } وهذا ممكن فيجب التصديق به فإن القادر على أن يطير الطير في الهواء قادر على أن يسير الإنسان على الصراط.", "english": "The Fifth Foundation: The Path (Al-Sirat) is a bridge extended over the back of Hellfire, thinner than a hair and sharper than a sword. Allah the Exalted said: 'So guide them to the path of Hellfire. And stop them; indeed, they are to be questioned.' {Surah As-Saffat: 23, 24} And this is possible, so belief in it is obligatory, for the One who is capable of making the bird fly in the air is capable of making the human walk on the Path.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Foundations of Belief", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter, from 'Foundations of Belief'", "badge": "Afterlife"}], "35": [{"arabic": "وذكر ذلك مطلقا في مواضع الترغيب ثم ذكر في بعض المواضع الصدق والإخلاص فقال مرة من قال لا إله إلا الله مخلصا ومعنى الإخلاص مساعدة الحال للمقال. فنسأل الله تعالى أن يجعلنا في الخاتمة من أهل لا إله إلا الله حالا ومقالا ظاهرا وباطنا حتى نودع الدنيا غير متلفتين إليها بل متبرمين بها ومحبين للقاء الله فإن من أحب لقاء الله تعالى أحب الله لقاءه ومن كره لقاء الله كره الله لقاءه فهذه مرامز إلى معاني الذكر التي لا يمكن الزيادة عليها في علم المعاملة. (الباب الثاني في آداب الدعاء وفضله وفضل بعض الأدعية المأثور", "english": "And he mentioned that absolutely in places of encouragement, then he mentioned in some places sincerity (Sidq) and purity of intention (Ikhlas), so he said once: 'Whoever says \"There is no god but Allah\" with purity of intention (Ikhlas), and the meaning of purity of intention (Ikhlas) is the state (Hal) assisting the statement (Maqal).' So we ask Allah the Exalted to make us at the conclusion among the people of \"There is no god but Allah\" in state (Hal) and statement (Maqal), outwardly and inwardly, until we bid farewell to the world not attached to it but rather weary of it and loving the meeting with Allah. For whoever loves the meeting with Allah the Exalted, Allah loves meeting him, and whoever hates the meeting with Allah, Allah hates meeting him. These are indications to the meanings of the remembrance (Dhikr) which cannot be increased upon in the science of interaction. (Chapter Two on the Etiquettes of Supplication and its Virtue and the Virtue of Some Transmitted Supplications and the Virtue of Seeking Forgiveness and Sending Blessings on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ) (The Virtue of Supplication) Allah the Exalted said: 'And when My servants ask you concerning Me, indeed I am near. I respond to the invocation of the supplicant when he calls upon Me.' {} And He the Exalted said: 'Invoke your Lord in humility and secretly; indeed, He does not like transgressors.' {} And He the Exalted said: 'And your Lord says, \"Call upon Me; I will respond to you. Indeed, those who are arrogant (Yastakbirun) toward My worship will enter Hell in humiliation.\"' {} And He the Mighty and Majestic said: 'Say, \"Call upon Allah or call upon the Most Merciful. Whichever [name] you call - to Him belong the best names.\"' {} And Nu'man bin Bashir narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: 'Supplication is worship, then he recited: \"Call upon Me; I will respond to you.\"' {} the verse. And he ﷺ said: 'Supplication is the marrow of worship.' And Abu Hurairah narrated that he ﷺ said: 'There is nothing more honorable to Allah the Mighty and Majestic than supplication.' And he ﷺ said: 'Indeed, the servant does not'", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-9.doc.txt", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "ومثل هذا الشخص هو البائع للدنيا بالآخرة وحالة الشهيد توافق معنى قولك لا إله إلا الله فإنه لا مقصود له سوى الله عز وجل وكل مقصود معبود وكل معبود إله فهذا الشهيد قائل بلسان حاله لا إله إلا الله إذ لا مقصود له سواه ومن يقول ذلك بلسانه ولم يساعده حاله فأمره في مشيئة الله عز وجل ولا يؤمن في حقه الخطر ولذلك فضل رسول الله ﷺ قول لا إله إلا الله على سائر الأذكار وذكر ذلك مطلقا في مواضع الترغيب ثم ذكر في بعض المواضع الصدق والإخلاص فقال مرة من قال لا إله إلا الله مخلصا ومعنى الإخلاص مساعدة الحال للمقال. فن", "english": "And such a person is the seller of the worldly life (Dunya) for the Hereafter (Akhirah), and the state of the martyr (Shahid) corresponds to the meaning of your saying 'There is no god but Allah (La ilaha illa Allah)', for he has no objective (Maqsud) except Allah the Exalted, and every objective is worshipped (Ma'bud), and every worshipped one is a god (Ilah). So this martyr is saying with the tongue of his state (Lisan al-Hal) 'There is no god but Allah', since he has no objective other than Him. And whoever says that with his tongue but his state (Hal) does not assist it, his affair is in the will of Allah the Exalted, and danger is not secured in his right. And for that reason, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ preferred the saying 'There is no god but Allah' over all other remembrances (Adhkar), and he mentioned that absolutely in places of encouragement. Then he mentioned in some places truthfulness (Sidq) and sincerity (Ikhlas), saying once: 'Whoever says 'There is no god but Allah' sincerely (Mukhlisan)', and the meaning of sincerity is the assistance of the state (Hal) to the statement (Maqal). So we ask Allah the Exalted to make us in the ending (Khatimah) from the people of 'There is no god but Allah' in state (Hal) and statement (Maqal), outwardly (Zahiran) and inwardly (Batinan), until we bid farewell to the worldly life (Dunya) not turning back to it, but rather being weary of it and loving the meeting with Allah. For whoever loves the meeting with Allah the Exalted, Allah loves meeting him, and whoever hates the meeting with Allah, Allah hates meeting him. These are indications to the meanings of the remembrance (Dhikr) that cannot be increased upon in the science of interaction (Ilm al-Mu'amalah).", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-9.doc.txt", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "وأما الآثار؛ فقد جاء في الأثر: لا تزال لا إله إلا الله تدفع عن العباد سخط الله عز وجل ما لم يسألوا ما نقص من دنياهم. وفي لفظ آخر: ما لم يؤثروا صفقة دنياهم على دينهم، فإذا فعلوا ذلك وقالوا: لا إله إلا الله، قال الله تعالى: كذبتم، لستم بها صادقين.", "english": "As for the narrations; it has come in the narration: 'The declaration \"There is no god but Allah\" (La ilaha illa Allah) continues to ward off from the servants the wrath of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, as long as they do not ask for what diminishes from their worldly life.' And in another wording: 'As long as they do not prefer the transaction of their worldly life over their religion, so if they do that and say: \"There is no god but Allah,\" Allah, the Exalted, says: \"You have lied, you are not truthful in it.\"'", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book4.doc.txt", "book_title": "Poverty and Abstinence", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Poverty and Abstinence'", "badge": "Ethics"}, {"arabic": "وقال ﷺ: (الباقيات الصالحات هن لا إله إلا الله وسبحان الله والحمد لله والله أكبر ولا حول ولا قوة إلا بالله[37]) وقال ﷺ: (ما على الأرض رجل يقول لا إله إلا الله والله أكبر وسبحان الله والحمد لله ولا حول ولا قوة إلا بالله إلا غفرت ذنوبه ولو كانت مثل زبد البحر[38]) رواه ابن عمر وروى النعمان بن بشير عنه ﷺ أنه قال: (الذين يذكرون من جلال الله وتسبيحه وتكبيره وتحميده ينعطفن حول العرش لهن دوى كدوي النحل يذكرون بصاحبهن أو لا يحب أحدكم أن لا يزال عند الله ما يذكر به[39]) وروى أبو هريرة أنه ﷺ قال: (لأن أقول ", "english": "And he (peace be upon him) said: (The enduring righteous deeds are: There is no god but Allah, and glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and Allah is the greatest, and there is no power nor strength except with Allah [37]). And he (peace be upon him) said: (There is no man on earth who says: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is the greatest, and glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no power nor strength except with Allah, except that his sins are forgiven, even if they were like the foam of the sea [38]) narrated by Ibn Umar. And Nu'man bin Bashir narrated from him (peace be upon him) that he said: (Those who remember from the majesty of Allah and His glorification, magnification, and praise, they circle around the Throne, having a humming like the humming of bees, remembering their companion; or does not one of you love that there remains with Allah what he is remembered by [39]). And Abu Hurairah narrated that he (peace be upon him) said: (For me to say: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is the greatest, is more beloved to me than what the sun has risen upon [40]). And in another narration, he added: There is no power nor strength except with Allah, and he said it is better than the world and what is in it. And he (peace be upon him) said: (The most beloved speech to Allah the Exalted are four: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is the greatest; it does not harm you with which of them you begin [41]) narrated by Samurah bin Jundub. And Abu Malik al-Ash'ari narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to say: (Purity is half of faith, and praise be to Allah fills the scale, and glory be to Allah and Allah is the greatest fill what is between the heaven and the earth, and prayer is light, and charity is proof, and patience is illumination, and the Quran is an argument for you or against you, every).", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-9.doc.txt", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications and their spiritual significance", "badge": "Du'a"}, {"arabic": "لشيء وإلي يعود العزيز الحكيم الرحمن الرحيم مالك يوم الدين خالق الخير والشر خالق الجنة والنار الواحد الأحد الفرد الصمد الذي لم يتخذ صاحبة ولا ولدا الفرد الوتر عالم الغيب والشهادة الملك القدوس السلام المؤمن المهيمن العزيز الجبار المتكبر الخالق البارىء المصور الكبير المتعال المقتدر القهار الحليم الكريم أهل الثناء والمجد أعلم السر وأخفى القادر الرزاق فوق الخلق والخليقة[135]). وذكر قبل كل كلمة إني أنا الله لا إله إلا أنا كما أوردناه في الأول فمن دعا بهذه الأسماء فليقل إنك أنت الله لا إله إلا أنت كذا ", "english": "To something and to Him returns the Mighty, the Wise, the Compassionate, the Merciful, Owner of the Day of Judgment, Creator of good and evil, Creator of Paradise and Hell, the One, the Unique, the Solitary, the Eternal, who has not taken a companion nor a son, the Single, the Odd, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, the King, the Holy, the Peace, the Faithful, the Guardian, the Mighty, the Compeller, the Proud, the Creator, the Originator, the Fashioner, the Great, the Exalted, the Powerful, the Subduer, the Forbearing, the Generous, Worthy of praise and glory, Knower of the secret and what is more hidden, the Able, the Provider above creation and creatures [135]). And mention before every word 'Indeed I am Allah, there is no god except Me' as we brought it in the first, so whoever supplicates with these names, let him say 'Indeed You are Allah, there is no god except You' such and such, so whoever supplicates with them is written among the prostrating, the humble ones who will be neighbors to Muhammad, Abraham, Moses, Jesus, and the prophets, prayers of Allah be upon them, in the abode of majesty, and for him is the reward of the worshippers in the heavens and the earths, and may Allah bless Muhammad and every chosen servant. (Supplication of Ibn al-Mu'tamir, who is Sulayman al-Taymi, and his glorifications, may Allah be pleased with him) It was narrated that Yunus ibn 'Ubayd saw a man in a dream from those killed as martyrs in the lands of the Romans, and he said: 'What is the best thing you have seen then from the deeds?' He said: 'I saw the glorifications of Ibn al-Mu'tamir from Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, in a place, and they are these: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god except Allah, and Allah is greater, and there is no power nor strength except with Allah, the High, the Great, as much as what He created, and the number of what He is creating, and the weight of what He created, and the weight of what He is creating, and the fullness of what He created, and the fullness of what He is creating, and the fullness of His heavens, and the fullness of His earth, and the like of that, and multiples of that, and the number of His creation, and the weight of His Throne, and the extent of His mercy, and the ink of His words, and the extent of His pleasure until He is pleased, and when He is pleased, and the number of what His creation has mentioned Him with in all that has passed, and the number of what they will mention Him with in what remains in every year, month, week, day, night, hour from the hours, breath and breath from the breaths, and eternity from the eternities, from eternity to eternity, eternity of the world and eternity of the Hereafter, and more than that, its beginning does not cease and its end does not end.' (Supplication of Ibrahim ibn Adham, may Allah be pleased with him) It was narrated that Ibrahim ibn Bashar, his servant, said that he would say this supplication every Friday when he became morning and when he became evening: 'Welcome to the day of increase and the new morning, and the writer and the witness, our day today is a day of Eid, write for us in it what we say: In the name of Allah, the Praised, the Glorious, the Exalted, the Loving, the Doer in His creation what He wills. I have become morning believing in Allah, and believing in meeting Him, and acknowledging His proof, and seeking forgiveness from my sin, and submitting to the lordship of Allah, and denying other than Allah among the gods, and to Allah poor, and upon Allah relying, and to Allah turning. I bear witness to Allah and I bear witness to His angels, His prophets, His messengers, and bearers...'", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-9.doc.txt", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter", "badge": "Afterlife"}], "40": [{"arabic": "وعند هذا زل أقدام الأكثرون إلا عباد الله المخلصين الذين لا سلطان عليهم للشيطان اللعين فشاهدوا بنور البصائر كون الكاتب مسخراً مضطراً، كما شاهد جميع الضعفاء كون القلم مسخراً، وعرفوا أن غلط الضعفاء في ذلك كغلط النملة مثلاً لو كانت تدب على الكاغد فترى رأس القلم يسود الكاغد، ولم يمتد بصرها إلى اليد والأصابع فضلاً عن صاحب اليد فغلطت وظنت القلم هو المسود للبياض، وذلك لقصور بصرها عن مجاوزة رأس القلم لضيق حدقتها، فكذلك من لم ينشرح بنور الله تعالى صدره للإسلام قصرت عن ملاحظة جبار السموات والأرض ومشاهدة كو", "english": "And at this point, the feet of most people slipped except the purified servants (Ibad Allah al-Mukhlaseen) of Allah upon whom the accursed Satan has no authority, for they witnessed with the light of insight (Basa'ir) that the writer is a compelled instrument (Musakhkharan Mudtarran), just as all the weak witnessed that the pen is an instrument. And they knew that the mistake of the weak in that is like the mistake of an ant, for example, if it were crawling on the paper and sees the tip of the pen blackening the paper, and its sight did not extend to the hand and the fingers, let alone the owner of the hand, so it erred and thought the pen is what blackens the whiteness, and that is due to the deficiency of its sight from surpassing the tip of the pen because of the narrowness of its pupil. Likewise, he whose chest (Sadr) has not expanded with the light of Allah the Exalted for Islam (Islam) fell short from observing the Compeller (Jabbar) of the heavens and the earth and witnessing His being overpowering behind everything, so he stopped on the path at the writer, and that is pure ignorance. Rather, the possessors of hearts (Arbab al-Qulub) and spiritual visions (Mushahadat) - Allah the Exalted has made every particle in the heavens and the earth speak in their regard by His power (Qudrah) with which everything speaks, until they heard its glorification (Tasbih) and sanctification (Taqdis) for Allah the Exalted and its testimony against itself of incapacity (Ajz) with an eloquent tongue (Lisan Dhalq) that speaks without letter (Harf) nor sound (Sawt) that those who are isolated from hearing (Sam') do not hear. And I do not mean by it the apparent hearing (Sam' al-Zahir) that does not exceed sounds, for the donkey shares in it, and there is no value for what the beasts share in. Rather, I intend by it a hearing (Sam') that perceives thereby a speech (Kalam) that is not by letter nor sound, nor is it Arabic nor non-Arabic.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book5.doc.txt", "book_title": "Monotheism and Reliance", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Monotheism and Reliance'", "badge": "Insight"}], "61": [{"arabic": "وقيل فتح عبد الله بن المبارك عينه عند الوفاة وضحك وقال: ﴿ لمثل هذا فليعمل العاملون ﴾ {} ولما حضرت إبراهيم النخعي الوفاة بكى فقيل له ما يبكيك قال انتظر من الله رسولا يبشرني بالجنة أو بالنار", "english": "And it was said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak opened his eyes at the time of death and laughed and said: 'For the like of this let the workers work.' {} And when the death of Ibrahim al-Nakha'i approached, he wept, so it was said to him: 'What makes you weep?' He said: 'I await from Allah a messenger to give me glad tidings of Paradise or the Fire.'", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Repentance", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter, from 'Book of Repentance'", "badge": "Afterlife"}, {"arabic": "وعن ابن عيينة قال رأيت سفيان الثوري في النوم كأنه في الجنة يطير من شجرة إلى شجرة يقول لمثل هذا فليعمل العاملون فقلت له أوصني قال أقلل من معرفة الناس", "english": "And from Ibn 'Uyaynah, he said: I saw Sufyan al-Thawri in a dream as if he were in Paradise, flying from tree to tree, saying: 'For the like of this let the workers work.' So I said to him: 'Advise me.' He said: 'Reduce your acquaintance with people.'", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Repentance", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter, from 'Book of Repentance'", "badge": "Afterlife"}], "64": [{"arabic": "ثم انظر إلى طعامهم وهو الزقوم كما قال الله تعالى: ﴿ ثم إنكم إيها الضالون المكذبون لآكلون من شجر من زقوم فمالئون منها البطون فشاربون عليه من الحميم فشاربون شرب الهيم ﴾ {} وقال تعالى: ﴿ إنها شجرة تخرج فى أصل الجحيم طلعها كأنه رءوس الشياطين فإنهم لآكلون منها فمالئون منها البطون ثم إن لهم عليها لشوبا من حميم ثم إن مرجعهم لإلى الجحيم ﴾ {}", "english": "Then look at their food, which is the Zaqqum (Zaqqum) as Allah the Exalted said: 'Then indeed you, O those astray and deniers, will eat from a tree of Zaqqum and fill your bellies with it, then drink on top of it from boiling water, drinking like thirsty camels.' And He the Exalted said: 'Indeed it is a tree that emerges in the foundation of the Hellfire (al-Jahim), its fruit as if it were heads of devils. Then indeed they will eat from it and fill their bellies with it, then indeed for them upon it is a mixture of boiling water, then indeed their return is to the Hellfire (al-Jahim).'", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Repentance", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter, from 'Book of Repentance'", "badge": "Afterlife"}], "74": [{"arabic": "وعند هذا زل أقدام الأكثرون إلا عباد الله المخلصين الذين لا سلطان عليهم للشيطان اللعين فشاهدوا بنور البصائر كون الكاتب مسخراً مضطراً، كما شاهد جميع الضعفاء كون القلم مسخراً، وعرفوا أن غلط الضعفاء في ذلك كغلط النملة مثلاً لو كانت تدب على الكاغد فترى رأس القلم يسود الكاغد، ولم يمتد بصرها إلى اليد والأصابع فضلاً عن صاحب اليد فغلطت وظنت القلم هو المسود للبياض، وذلك لقصور بصرها عن مجاوزة رأس القلم لضيق حدقتها، فكذلك من لم ينشرح بنور الله تعالى صدره للإسلام قصرت عن ملاحظة جبار السموات والأرض ومشاهدة كو", "english": "And at this point, the feet of most people slipped except the purified servants (Ibad Allah al-Mukhlaseen) of Allah upon whom the accursed Satan has no authority, for they witnessed with the light of insights (Basa'ir) that the writer is a compelled instrument (Musakhkhar), just as all the weak witnessed that the pen is an instrument. And they knew that the error of the weak in this is like the error of an ant, for example, if it were crawling on the paper and saw the tip of the pen blackening the paper, and its sight did not extend to the hand and fingers, let alone the possessor of the hand, so it erred and thought the pen was the one blackening the whiteness, and that is due to the deficiency of its sight from surpassing the tip of the pen because of the narrowness of its pupil. Similarly, whoever's chest (Sadr) was not expanded by the light of Allah, the Exalted, for Islam (Islam), his sight fell short from observing the Compeller (Jabbar) of the heavens and the earth and witnessing His being the Dominator (Qahir) behind everything, so he stopped on the path at the writer, and that is pure ignorance. Rather, the possessors of hearts (Qulub) and spiritual visions (Mushahadat) - Allah, the Exalted, has made every particle in the heavens and the earth speak in their regard by His power (Qudrah) through which everything speaks, until they heard its glorification (Tasbih) and sanctification (Taqdis) for Allah, the Exalted, and its testimony against itself of incapacity (Ajz) with a fluent tongue (Lisan Dhalq) that speaks without letter (Harf) or sound (Sawt), which those who are isolated from hearing (Sam') do not hear. And I do not mean by it the apparent hearing (Sam' al-Dhahir) that does not transcend sounds, for the donkey shares in it, and there is no value in what the beasts share in. Rather, I intend by it a hearing (Sam') that perceives a speech (Kalam) that is not by letter nor sound, nor is it Arabic nor non-Arabic.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book5.doc.txt", "book_title": "Monotheism and Reliance", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Monotheism and Reliance'", "badge": "Insight"}], "96": [{"arabic": "الأصل الأول: العلم بأن كل حادث في العالم فهو فعله وخلقه واختراعه لا خالق له سواه ولا محدث له إلا إياه خلق الخلق وصنعهم وأوجد قدرتهم وحركتهم فجميع أفعال عباده مخلوقة له ومتعلقة بقدرته تصديقا له في قوله تعالى الله خالق كل شيء وفي قوله تعالى والله خلقكم وما تعملون وفي قوله تعالى وأسروا قولكم أو اجهروا به إنه عليم بذات الصدور ألا يعلم من خلق وهو اللطيف الخبير أمر العباد بالتحرز في أقوالهم وأفعالهم وإسرارهم وإضمارهم لعلمه بموارد أفعالهم واستدل على العلم بالخلق وكيف لا يكون خالقا لفعل العبد وقدرته تام", "english": "The First Principle: The knowledge that every occurrence in the world is His action, His creation, and His invention; there is no creator for it other than Him, and no one brings it into existence except Him. He created the creation and fashioned them, brought into existence their power (Qudrah) and their movement, so all the actions of His servants are created by Him and connected to His power (Qudrah), confirming Him in His saying, the Exalted: 'Allah is the Creator of everything' and in His saying: 'And Allah created you and what you do' and in His saying: 'And conceal your speech or proclaim it, indeed He is Knowing of what is within the chests. Does He not know who He created? And He is the Subtle, the Aware.' He commanded the servants to be cautious in their statements and their actions, their secrets and their hidden thoughts due to His knowledge of the sources of their actions, and He argued for the knowledge of creation. And how could He not be the creator of the servant's action when His power (Qudrah) is complete with no deficiency in it, and it is connected to the movement of the bodies of the servants, and the movements are similar, and the connection of the power (Qudrah) to them is for their essence. So what is it that restricts its connection from some movements without others despite their similarity? Or how could the animal be independent in invention when there issues from the spider, the bee, and all the animals from subtle crafts what bewilders the intellects of those of understanding? So how did they become isolated in their invention without the Lord of lords, and they are not knowing of the details of what issues from them of acquisition? Far, far be it! The creations have been humbled, and He is unique in sovereignty and dominion, the Compeller of the earth and the heavens.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Foundations of Belief", "content_type": "general", "topic": "Commentary from Al-Ghazali's Ihya 'Ulum al-Din, from 'Foundations of Belief'", "badge": "General"}], "99": [{"arabic": "فهؤلاء جميع أحوالهم تصلح أن تكون سببا لازيادهم فلا تتميز عندهم عبادة عن عبادة وهم الذين فروا إلى الله عز وجل كما قال تعالى: ﴿ لعلكم تذكرون ﴾ {} ففروا إلى الله وتحقق فيهم قوله تعالى: ﴿ وإذ اعتزلتموهم وما يعبدون إلا الله فأووا إلى الكهف ينشر لكم ربكم من رحمته ﴾ {} وإليه الإشارة بقوله: ﴿ إني ذاهب إلى ربي سيهدين ﴾ {} وهذه منتهى درجات الصديقين ولا وصول إليها إلا بعد ترتيب الأوراد والمواظبة عليها دهرا طويلا فلا ينبغي أن يغتر المريد بما سمعه من ذلك فيدعيه لنفسه ويفتر عن وظائف عبادته فذلك علامته أن لا ي", "english": "For these people, all their states become a cause for their increase, so no worship is distinguished from another worship for them, and they are those who have fled to Allah the Exalted, as He said: 'That you may remember' (Quran 2:203), so flee to Allah. And His saying is realized in them: 'And when you withdraw from them and that which they worship except Allah, then take refuge in the cave; your Lord will spread for you of His mercy' (Quran 18:16). And to this is the indication by His saying: 'Indeed, I am going to my Lord; He will guide me' (Quran 37:99). And this is the utmost degree of the truthful ones (Siddiqin), and there is no reaching it except after arranging the litanies (Awrad) and persisting in them for a long time. So it is not fitting for the seeker (Murid) to be deceived by what he hears of that and claim it for himself and slacken from the duties of his worship. Its sign is that no whisper (Waswas) occurs in his heart (Qalb), and no sin (Ma'siyah) crosses his heart (Qalb), and the assaults of terrors (Hawal) do not agitate him, nor do great affairs (Ashghal) startle him. And how is this rank granted to everyone? So it is incumbent upon all to arrange the litanies (Awrad) as we have mentioned.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Knowledge", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Book of Knowledge'", "badge": "Insight"}], "128": [{"arabic": "وعند هذا زل أقدام الأكثرون إلا عباد الله المخلصين الذين لا سلطان عليهم للشيطان اللعين فشاهدوا بنور البصائر كون الكاتب مسخراً مضطراً، كما شاهد جميع الضعفاء كون القلم مسخراً، وعرفوا أن غلط الضعفاء في ذلك كغلط النملة مثلاً لو كانت تدب على الكاغد فترى رأس القلم يسود الكاغد، ولم يمتد بصرها إلى اليد والأصابع فضلاً عن صاحب اليد فغلطت وظنت القلم هو المسود للبياض، وذلك لقصور بصرها عن مجاوزة رأس القلم لضيق حدقتها، فكذلك من لم ينشرح بنور الله تعالى صدره للإسلام قصرت عن ملاحظة جبار السموات والأرض ومشاهدة كو", "english": "At this point, the feet of most people slipped except the purified servants (Ibad Allah al-Mukhlaseen) of Allah upon whom the accursed Satan has no authority, for they witnessed with the light of insight (Basa'ir) that the writer is a compelled instrument (Musakhkhar), just as all the weak witnessed that the pen is an instrument. They recognized that the error of the weak in this is like the error of an ant, for example, if it were crawling on the paper and saw the tip of the pen blackening the paper, and its sight did not extend to the hand and fingers, let alone the owner of the hand, so it erred and thought the pen was the one blackening the whiteness, due to the deficiency of its sight from exceeding the tip of the pen because of the narrowness of its pupil. Similarly, whoever's chest (Sadr) has not expanded with the light of Allah the Exalted for Islam (Islam), their sight fell short from observing the Compeller (Jabbar) of the heavens and the earth and witnessing His being the Dominant (Qahir) behind everything, so they stopped on the path at the writer, which is pure ignorance. Rather, the possessors of hearts (Qulub) and spiritual visions (Mushahadat) - Allah the Exalted has made every particle in the heavens and the earth speak in their regard by His power (Qudrah) through which everything speaks, until they heard its glorification (Tasbih) and sanctification (Taqdis) for Allah the Exalted and its testimony against itself of incapacity with a fluent tongue (Lisan Dhalq) that speaks without letter (Harf) or sound (Sawt), which those who are isolated from hearing (Sam') do not hear. I do not mean by it the apparent hearing (Sam' al-Zahir) that does not exceed sounds, for the donkey shares in it, and there is no value in what the beasts share in. Rather, I intend by it a hearing (Sam') that perceives a speech (Kalam) that is not by letter nor sound, nor is it Arabic nor non-Arabic.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book5.doc.txt", "book_title": "Monotheism and Reliance", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Monotheism and Reliance'", "badge": "Insight"}], "130": [{"arabic": "ومنها المنقول المنقلب كقوله تعالى ﴿ وطور سينين ﴾ {} أي طور سيناء ﴿ سلام على إل ياسين ﴾ {} أي على الياس وقيل إدريس لأن في حرف ابن مسعود سلام على إدراسين", "english": "And among them is the transferred and reversed, like His saying, the Exalted: 'And Mount Sinai (Ṭūr Sīnīn)' meaning Mount Sinai (Ṭūr Sīnā'), 'Peace be upon the family of Yasin (Salam 'alā Āl Yāsīn)' meaning upon Elias (Ilyās), and it is said Idris (Idrīs) because in the reading of Ibn Mas'ud it is 'Peace be upon Idrasin (Salam 'alā Idrāsīn)'.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-8.doc.txt", "book_title": "Etiquette of Quran Recitation", "content_type": "fiqh", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the outer and inner dimensions of worship, from 'Etiquette of Quran Recitation'", "badge": "Worship"}], "137": [{"arabic": "وعلى القعود عن هذا السفر وقع الإنكار بقوله تعالى وإنكم لتمرون عليهم مصبحين وبالليل أفلا تعقلون وبقوله سبحانه وكأين من آية في السماوات والأرض يمرون عليها وهم عنها معرضون", "english": "And upon the abstention from this journey falls the reproach by His saying, the Exalted: 'And indeed, you pass by them in the morning and by night - will you not then use intellect?' and by His saying, the Glorified: 'And how many a sign in the heavens and the earth do they pass by while they are turning away from it?'", "book_file": "vol2_j2-k07.doc.txt", "book_title": "Etiquette of Travel", "content_type": "dhikr", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the virtue and practice of remembering God, from 'Etiquette of Travel'", "badge": "Dhikr"}], "147": [{"arabic": "وقال أبو هريرة لو كان فى المسجد مائة ألف أو يزيدون ثم تنفس رجل من أهل النار لماتوا وقد قال بعض العلماء فى قوله: ﴿ تلفح وجوههم النار ﴾ {} إنها لفحتهم لفحة واحدة فما أبقت لحما على عظم إلا ألقته عند أعقابهم", "english": "And Abu Huraira said: 'If there were in the mosque one hundred thousand or more (mā'at alf aw yazīdūn), then a man from the people of the Fire breathed, they would die.' And some scholars said regarding His saying: 'The Fire will scorch their faces' {} that it scorches them with one scorching, and it leaves no flesh upon a bone except that it casts it at their heels.'", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Repentance", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter, from 'Book of Repentance'", "badge": "Afterlife"}], "160": [{"arabic": "وعند هذا زل أقدام الأكثرون إلا عباد الله المخلصين الذين لا سلطان عليهم للشيطان اللعين فشاهدوا بنور البصائر كون الكاتب مسخراً مضطراً، كما شاهد جميع الضعفاء كون القلم مسخراً، وعرفوا أن غلط الضعفاء في ذلك كغلط النملة مثلاً لو كانت تدب على الكاغد فترى رأس القلم يسود الكاغد، ولم يمتد بصرها إلى اليد والأصابع فضلاً عن صاحب اليد فغلطت وظنت القلم هو المسود للبياض، وذلك لقصور بصرها عن مجاوزة رأس القلم لضيق حدقتها، فكذلك من لم ينشرح بنور الله تعالى صدره للإسلام قصرت عن ملاحظة جبار السموات والأرض ومشاهدة كو", "english": "And at this point, the feet of most people slipped except the purified servants (Ibad Allah al-Mukhlaseen) of Allah upon whom the accursed Satan has no authority, so they witnessed with the light of insight (Basa'ir) that the writer is a compelled and subjugated one, just as all the weak ones witnessed that the pen is subjugated. And they knew that the mistake of the weak ones in that is like the mistake of an ant, for example, if it were crawling on the paper and sees the tip of the pen blackening the paper, and its sight did not extend to the hand and the fingers, let alone the possessor of the hand, so it erred and thought the pen is the one that blackens the whiteness, and that is due to the deficiency of its sight from surpassing the tip of the pen because of the narrowness of its pupil. Likewise, he whose chest (Sadr) has not expanded with the light of Allah the Exalted for Islam (Islam), his sight fell short from observing the Compeller of the heavens and the earth and witnessing His being the Dominant behind everything, so he stopped on the way at the writer, and that is pure ignorance. Rather, the possessors of hearts (Qulub) and spiritual visions (Mushahadat) - Allah the Exalted has made every particle in the heavens and the earth speak on their behalf by His power (Qudrah) with which everything speaks, until they heard its glorification and its praise (Tasbih) of Allah the Exalted and its testimony against itself of incapacity with a fluent tongue that speaks without letter (Harf) or sound (Sawt) that is not heard by those who are isolated from hearing (Sam'). And I do not mean by it the apparent hearing (Sam' al-Zahir) that does not go beyond sounds, for the donkey shares in it, and there is no value for that in which beasts share. Rather, I intend by it a hearing (Sam') that perceives thereby a speech (Kalam) that is not by letter nor sound, nor is it Arabic nor non-Arabic.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book5.doc.txt", "book_title": "Monotheism and Reliance", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Monotheism and Reliance'", "badge": "Insight"}], "164": [{"arabic": "فإن ما رزق تعالى الملائكة من القرب والرتبة لازم مستمر على حال واحد لا يزيد ولا ينقص لذلك أخبر الله عنهم أنهم قالوا: وما منا إلا له مقام معلوم، وفارق الإنسان الملائكة في الترقي من درجة إلى درجة فإنه لا يزال يتقرب إلى الله تعالى فيستفيد مزيد قربه وباب المزيد مسدود على الملائكة عليهم السلام وليس لكل واحد إلا رتبته التي هي وقف عليه وعبادته التي هو مشغول بها لا ينتقل إلى غيرها ولا يفتر عنها لا يستكبرون عن عبادته ولا يستحسرون يسبحون الليل والنهار لا يفترون ومفتاح مزيد الدرجات هي الصلوات.", "english": "For what Allah the Exalted has granted the angels of nearness and rank is constant and continuous in a single state that does not increase nor decrease; therefore, Allah informed about them that they said: 'And there is not among us except that he has a known station (maqām maʿlūm).' And the human differs from the angels in ascending from one degree to another, for he continuously draws nearer to Allah the Exalted and thus gains increased nearness, and the door of increase is closed upon the angels, peace be upon them. And for each one there is only his rank that is fixed upon him and his worship that he is occupied with; he does not transfer to other than it nor does he cease from it; they do not grow arrogant about worshipping Him nor do they become weary; they glorify night and day without ceasing, and the key to increased degrees is the prayers.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-4.doc.txt", "book_title": "Mysteries of Prayer", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Mysteries of Prayer'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "فاعلم أن خلقه الملائكة تخالف خلقة الإنس وما من واحد منهم إلا وهو وحدانى الصفة ليس فيه خلط وتركيب ألبتة فلا يكون لكل واحد منهم إلا فعل واحد، وإليه الإشارة بقوله تعالى: ﴿ وما منا إلا له مقام معلوم ﴾ {} فلذلك ليس بينهم تنافس وتقاتل بل مثالهم في تعين مرتبة كل واحد منهم وفعله مثال الحواس الخمس فإن البصر لا يزاحم السمع في إدراك الأصوات ولا الشم يزاحمها ولا هما يتنازعان الشم وليس كاليد والرجل فإنك قد تبطش بأصابع الرجل بطشا ضعيفا فتزاحم به اليد وقد تضرب غيرك برأسك فتزاحم اليد التى هى آلة الضرب ولا كالإن", "english": "Know that the creation of the angels differs from the creation of humans, and there is not one of them except that he is singular in attribute (وحدانى الصفة), with no mixing or composition whatsoever. Therefore, each one of them has only one action, and to this is the indication by His saying, the Exalted: 'And there is not among us except that he has a known station (مقام معلوم)' (Quran 37:164). Thus, there is no competition or fighting between them. Rather, their example in determining the rank of each one of them and his action is like the example of the five senses, for sight does not compete with hearing in perceiving sounds, nor does smell compete with them, nor do they dispute over smell. And it is not like the hand and the foot, for you may strike with the toes of the foot a weak strike, thus competing with the hand, and you may strike another with your head, thus competing with the hand which is the instrument of striking. Nor is it like the single human who undertakes by himself grinding, kneading, and baking, for this is a kind of deviation and departure from justice, its cause being the difference in the attributes (صفات) of the human and the difference in his motives (دواعيه). For he is not singular in attribute, so he is not singular in action. Therefore, we see the human obeying God at one time and disobeying Him at another due to the difference in his motives and attributes, and that is not possible in the nature (طباع) of the angels. Rather, they are molded upon obedience, peace be upon him, peace be upon him, peace be upon him, peace be upon him, peace be upon him. There is no room for disobedience in their right, so indeed they do not disobey God in what He commands them, and they do what they are commanded, and they glorify night and day without ceasing. The one bowing among them is bowing forever, the one prostrating among them is prostrating forever, and the one standing is standing forever. There is no difference in their actions nor slackness, and for each one there is a known station (مقام معلوم) which he does not exceed, and their obedience to God, the Exalted, from where there is no room for opposition in them, can be likened.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Patience and Gratitude", "content_type": "dhikr", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the virtue and practice of remembering God, from 'Patience and Gratitude'", "badge": "Dhikr"}], "171": [{"arabic": "والمغرورين فلا مانع لما أعطى ولا معطي لما منع ولم يقطع التوفيق عن الكفار لجناية متقدمة ولا أمد الأنبياء عليهم السلام بتوفيقه ونور هدايته لوسيلة سابقة ولكنه قال ولقد سبقت كلمتنا لعبادنا المرسلين وقال عز وجل ولكن حق القول مني لأملأن جهنم من الجنة والناس أجمعين وقال تعالى إن الذين سبقت لهم منا الحسنى أولئك عنها مبعدون فإن خطر ببالك أنه لم اختلفت السابقة وهم في ربقه العبودية مشتركون نوديت من سرادقات الجلال لا تجاوز حد الأدب فإنه لا يسئل عما يفعل وهم يسئلون", "english": "And the deluded ones, so there is no preventer for what He gives and no giver for what He withholds, and He did not cut off the Success (Tawfiq) from the disbelievers due to a preceding transgression, nor did He extend the Prophets, peace be upon them, with His Success (Tawfiq) and the light of His guidance due to a preceding means, but He said: 'And indeed Our Word (Kalimatuna) has preceded for Our servants, the messengers (al-Mursalin).' And He, the Exalted, said: 'But the true Word (al-Qawl) from Me is: I will fill Hell with jinn and mankind together.' And He, the Exalted, said: 'Indeed, those for whom the best (al-Husna) from Us has preceded, those are from it far removed.' So if it occurs to your mind that the preceding has not differed while they are in the bond of servitude (al-'ubudiyyah) sharing, you are called from the pavilions of Majesty: 'Do not exceed the limit of etiquette (al-Adab), for He is not questioned about what He does, but they will be questioned.'", "book_file": "vol2_j2-k08.doc.txt", "book_title": "Audition and Ecstasy", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions cited by Al-Ghazali with scholarly authentication, from 'Audition and Ecstasy'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "182": [{"arabic": "نجز كتاب الأذكار والدعوات بكماله يتلوه إن شاء الله تعالى كتاب الأوراد والحمد لله رب العالمين وصلى الله على سيدنا محمد وعلى آله وصحبه وسلم.", "english": "The Book of Remembrances (Adhkar) and Supplications (Dua'at) is completed in its entirety, to be followed, if Allah wills, by the Book of Regular Devotions (Awrad). And all praise (Al-Hamd) is for Allah, Lord (Rabb) of the worlds, and may Allah send blessings upon our master Muhammad and upon his family and companions and grant them peace.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-9.doc.txt", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications and their spiritual significance", "badge": "Du'a"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 350, 4076], [2, 4076, 5461]], "2": [[1, 250, 2048], [2, 2048, 3051]], "3": [[1, 250, 2141], [2, 2141, 3077]], "4": [[1, 350